On the other hand, a break and close above the 20-day EMA will be the first sign that the correction may be over. The buyers will then attempt to propel the pair to the psychological level at $100.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/decred-price-soars-45-in-one-day-three-weeks-before-a-major-hard-fork"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Decred price soars 45% in one day three weeks before a major hard fork}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT\par \par \uc2 Avalanche ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ) bounced off the uptrend line on April 15 but the failure to push the price above the moving averages may have attracted selling by the short-term traders. That pulled the price below the uptrend line today.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-04/42fcff79-c234-419f-b2dd-75e7264a8679.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price sustains below the uptrend line, the ascending triangle pattern will invalidate and the AVAX/USDT pair could drop to $65. If the price rebounds off this support, the pair could remain range-bound between $65 and $99 for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA ($81) and the RSI near 39 indicate that the path of least resistance is to the downside.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price rises and sustains above the uptrend line, it will suggest that the ascending triangle pattern remains intact. The bulls will then make one more attempt to push the price above the moving averages.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) turned down from $0.15 on April 15 indicating a lack of buying at higher levels. The price dipped back below the 20-day EMA ($0.14) on April 17 and has reached the 50-day SMA ($0.13).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-04/aa38ba39-246e-49de-a6f4-2c905d541a8d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If bears sink the price below the 50-day SMA, the DOGE/USDT pair could drop to the strong support at $0.12 and later to the psychological level at $0.10. The RSI has dipped into the negative zone, indicating a slight advantage to sellers.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price rebounds off the current level and rises above $0.15, the pair could attempt a rally to the 200-day SMA ($0.18). A break and close above this level could signal the start of a new up-move.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the overhead resistance at $19 on April 17, indicating that bears are selling on rallies to this level. The bears will now attempt to sink the price to the strong support at $16.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-04/78593ad0-46c2-48ce-b58a-879788dc5142.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($19) is sloping down and the RSI is below 40, suggesting that the momentum favors the bears. A break and close below $16 will be a huge negative as that could open the doors for a possible drop to $14.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price rebounds off $16, the bulls will again attempt to push the DOT/USDT pair above $19. If they manage to do that, the pair could continue its range-bound action between $16 and $23 for some more time.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDQvMTI3ZjM5YTItZjU3YS00YWRhLTkzN2UtZTRjMTU3YmYwMmY2LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220418ei4i000e1\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 4/15: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP, SOL,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , LUNA, AVAX, DOGE, DOT\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,825 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The failure of Bitcoin and altcoins to sustain the higher levels suggests that the sentiment remains negative and traders are selling on rallies.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) remains closely correlated with the S&P 500 but the institutional investors do not seem to be waiting for a turnaround in the United States' equities market or decoupling to happen before buying more Bitcoin.\par \par \uc2 Notably, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-institutional-buying-could-be-big-narrative-again-as-30k-btc-leaves-coinbase"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 30,000 Bitcoin moved out of Coinbase Pro}}}\uc2  in a single day, suggesting strong institutional demand.\par \par \uc2 MicroStrategy\uc2 , the publicly listed company which is the largest single-wallet holder of Bitcoin, does not seem to be content with its stash of 129,219 Bitcoin. In a letter to shareholders, the firm\u8217\'20\'19s CEO \uc2 Michael Saylor\uc2  said that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/microstrategy-shareholders-letter-we-ll-vigorously-pursue-more-btc-buys"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 company aims to \u8220\'20\'1Cvigorously pursue\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  and \u8220\'20\'1Cincrease awareness\u8221\'20\'1D about its Bitcoin strategy.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-04/778420f3-12d6-4f5d-8539-129c293aec7e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Another entity that has been at the forefront of Bitcoin purchases in the past few days has been the Luna Foundation Guard (LFG), a nonprofit organization attached to Terra, which owns 42,530 Bitcoin. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/terraform-labs-gifts-another-880m-to-luna-foundation-guard"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LFG was recently gifted $820 million}}}\uc2  worth of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/terra-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LUNA}}}\uc2  tokens by Terraform Labs, which some believe may be used to buy more Bitcoin.\par \par \uc2 Do the huge BTC outflows from a pro-trader crypto exchange suggest that a bottom may be close by? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s recovery fizzled out at $41,561 on April 13, indicating that higher levels continue to trigger selling. The buyers are currently attempting to defend {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-clings-to-40k-support-as-focus-returns-to-btc-price-supercycle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the psychological level at $40,000}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-04/0eb47d64-7120-421c-b148-d46b23c60caa.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day exponential moving average ($42,419) is sloping down and the relative strength index (RSI) is in the negative territory, indicating that the path of least resistance is to the downside.\par \par \uc2 If the price plummets below $39,200, the selling could intensify and the BTC/USDT pair could drop to the support line of the ascending channel. The bulls are likely to defend this level aggressively.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns up and breaks above the 20-day EMA, it will suggest accumulation at lower levels. The bulls will then attempt to push the pair to $45,400.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) has been sandwiched between the 20-day EMA ($3,144) and the 50-day simple moving average ($2,975) for the past three days. This suggests that bulls are defending the 50-day SMA while bears are selling on rallies to the 20-day EMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-04/b907a93a-2c0a-4da5-b3ca-b886e1be3894.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price breaks and sustains below $2,950, the selling could accelerate and the ETH/USDT pair could drop to $2,817. This level might act as a support but if it cracks, the next stop could be the uptrend line.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price rebounds off the current level and rises above the 20-day EMA, the pair could rally to the overhead zone between the 200-day SMA ($3,491) and $3,600. This is an important zone to watch out for because a break and close above it could signal the start of a new up-move.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) broke above the 20-day EMA ($420) on April 13 but the bulls could not build upon this advantage. The bears pulled the price back below the 20-day EMA on April 14 but a minor positive is that the bulls have not given up much ground.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-04/c2e8b2d7-4ba2-4810-9755-d8c0ac32f6a6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The flattish 20-day EMA and the RSI near the midpoint indicate a possible range-bound action in the near term. If the price rises above $427, the bulls will try to push the BNB/USDT pair to the 200-day SMA ($420) where the bears are expected to mount strong resistance.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the current level, the bears will try to sink the pair below $391. If they succeed, the decline could extend to the strong support at $350. The buyers are likely to defend this level with vigor.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s rebound picked up momentum and has reached the 50-day SMA ($0.78) today. If the price sustains above the 50-day SMA, the next stop could be the strong resistance at $0.91.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-04/425c34c0-5e70-46bf-ab02-bb1a1b47a9e9.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($0.77) is flattening out and the RSI is near the midpoint, indicating range-bound action in the near term. The XRP/USDT pair could remain stuck between $0.69 and $0.91 for the next few days.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the 50-day SMA, it will suggest that bears are selling on rallies. The pair could then drop to the critical level at $0.69. A break and close below this support could pull the pair down to $0.62.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) has been stuck between the 20-day EMA ($108) and the 50-day SMA ($100) for the past three days but this tight-range trading is unlikely to continue for long.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-04/18745d0c-03ae-48ca-9dab-a95ed1c10586.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If bears sink and sustain the price below the 50-day SMA, the selling could pick up momentum. The SOL/USDT pair could then decline to $86. The downsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI in the negative zone indicate advantage to sellers.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price rebounds off the 50-day SMA, the bulls will try to push the pair above the 20-day EMA. If they succeed, it will suggest that the correction may be over. The pair has a chance to then rise to $122 and later attempt a rally to the 200-day SMA ($148).\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) has been trading inside a tight range between $0.91 and $1 for the past three days. This suggests uncertainty about the next directional move.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-04/95c5ba77-8129-45da-9d62-00248f5c26f4.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA ($1) and the RSI in the negative territory indicate that bears are in command. If the tight range resolves to the downside, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could extend its decline to $0.86 and later to the critical support at $0.74.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns up from the current level and breaks above the 20-day EMA, the pair could rise to $1.10. A break and close above this minor resistance could open the doors for a possible retest of $1.26. The buyers will have to overcome this barrier to signal a potential change in trend.\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT\par \par \uc2 Terra\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/terra-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LUNA}}}\uc2  token turned down from $90 and broke below the support at $80 on April 14, indicating that bears are selling on every minor rally. The bears will now try to pull the price down to $75.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-04/72c73c34-4730-4dde-9e8b-a484bb1b80fe.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($94) and the 50-day SMA ($93) are about to complete a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI is in the negative territory, indicating that bears have the upper hand. A break and close below $75 could sink the LUNA/USDT pair to the 200-day SMA ($66). The bulls are expected to defend this level with all their might.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns up from the current level and breaks above the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the bears may be losing their grip. The pair could then attempt to rise above the psychological level at $100.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cardano-price-risks-30-drop-in-q2-despite-a-major-hard-fork-ahead"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cardano price risks 30% drop in Q2 despite a \u8216\'20\'18major\u8217\'20\'19 hard fork ahead}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT\par \par \uc2 Avalanche\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ) bounce off the uptrend line could not rise above the moving averages, indicating that the bears are active at higher levels. The price is currently stuck between the moving averages and the uptrend line.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-04/8f75cee5-e4ee-4acd-a27b-ed636dbc90f7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 This tight-range trading is unlikely to continue for long. The downsloping 20-day EMA ($83) and the RSI below 40 suggest that the bears have a slight edge. If the price turns down and breaks below the uptrend line, the selling could pick up momentum. The AVAX/USDT pair could then drop to the next support at $65.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price bounces off the uptrend line with strength, the buyers will try to push the pair above the moving averages. If they succeed, the pair could rise to $90 and later to $93.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 After two failed attempts to close above the 20-day EMA ($0.14) on April 12 and 13, the bulls managed to conquer the level on April 14. The buyers will now try to push Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) to $0.16 and then to the 200-day SMA ($0.18).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-04/23340f52-35b0-4933-98f2-e06c09adbda0.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears are likely to defend the 200-day SMA. If the price turns down from this resistance, it will suggest that the DOGE/USDT pair could remain stuck between the 50-day SMA ($0.13) and the 200-day SMA for a few days. The flat 20-day EMA and the RSI just above the midpoint also suggest a consolidation in the near term.\par \par \uc2 This view will be invalidated in the short term if the price turns down from the current level or the overhead resistance and plummets below the 50-day SMA. That could pull the pair down to $0.12.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 The recovery attempt in Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) lacks strength, indicating that demand dries up at higher levels. This increases the likelihood of the continuation of the correction.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-04/202572bb-9473-4bd5-8f90-17875f922d06.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA ($19) and the RSI in the negative zone indicate that bears have the upper hand. If the price turns down from the current level and breaks below $17, the decline could extend to $16. This level is likely to attract strong buying.\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off $16, the buyers will make another attempt to clear the overhead resistance at $19. If they succeed, it will suggest that the correction may be over. The DOT/USDT pair may then consolidate between $23 and $16 for some time.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price breaks below $16, the next stop should be the critical support at $14.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph.com. Every investment and trading move involves risk, you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDQvYjE4MjVjNjgtOGVlNi00YTkxLTkxNjYtNzc2YThhZDA0NzZiLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220415ei4f0008d\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Bitcoin retains $41K as BTC exchange withdrawals match record levels\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By William Suberg \par \uc2 547 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 April 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 BTC price performance edges into stronger territory while Bitcoin exchanges see major buy demand.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) held on to fresh gains on April 14 after a rebound in line with April 13\u8217\'20\'19s Wall Street open flipped the mood.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-04/53e6d6e4-0272-4068-9e3f-1892bac8645f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD 1-hour candle chart (\uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 ). Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 $40,500 now the level to hold\par \par \uc2 Data from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.cointelegraph.com/?via=markets&_ga=2.142027444.742658523.1640948929-762064149.1640948929"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cointelegraph Markets Pro}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSD/?exchange=BINANCE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\uc2  showed BTC/USD still trading above $41,000 April 14, having {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-bounces-to-near-41k-after-crypto-sentiment-gauge-hits-6-week-lows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reclaimed the $40,000 mark}}}\uc2  during the move higher.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo far so good, I expected a move to 41K but I doubt about going for an extra leg down to the green box (blue),\u8221\'20\'1D popular trader Crypto Ed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Crypto_Ed_NL/status/1514307438262067208"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 commented}}}\uc2  overnight alongside a chart with near-term price targets.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CComing hours a bit more up, followed by a correction. Retest of 40.5K and when that holds, we'll go for 42K\u8211\'20\'1343K (white). Lose 40.5K and we'll go for [the] green box.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-04/99352290-d15a-444d-b902-f21fdaa57e53.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD chart. Source: Crypto Ed/ \uc2 Twitter\par \par \uc2 At the time of writing, $40,500 showed no signs of falling, with \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  ebbing into April 14 and Bitcoin seeing no major threat to its bounce.\par \par \uc2 Zooming out, others took the opportunity to argue that despite the lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment, Bitcoin, itself, was far from \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Bitcoin?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Bitcoin}}}\uc2  has been in an uptrend on the daily time frame for nearly 3 months: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/N3EVgVsj27"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/N3EVgVsj27}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Matthew Hyland (@MatthewHyland_) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MatthewHyland_/status/1514387005039423492?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The lower the time preference, the less cause for panic \u8212\'20\'14 year to year, fellow analyst TechDev demonstrated, Bitcoin had more than a passing resemblance to traditional market behavior, even after dropping over 50% from November's all-time highs.\par \par \uc2 In focus this month was a similar chart pattern between Bitcoin now and the Dow Jones from the start of the 1990s.\par \par \uc2 "Times change. Assets change. Macro aggregate human behavior usually doesn't," TechDev {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TechDev_52/status/1514356397051367424/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 summarized}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin's stocks correlation is nonetheless a cause for concern for some, with a drawdown tipped to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://editorial.space/articles/14507"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 impact price significantly}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Exchange withdrawals heat up\par \par \uc2 For Blockware lead insights analyst William Clemente, meanwhile, there were other reasons to keep the faith.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/price-analysis-4-13-btc-eth-bnb-sol-xrp-ada-luna-avax-dot-doge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 4/13: BTC, ETH, BNB, SOL, XRP, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , LUNA, AVAX, DOT, DOGE}}}\par \par \uc2 Cryptocurrency exchanges were losing BTC reserves at a rate rarely seen before, he noted on April 13, implying that any rise in demand would compete with a rapidly-dwindling supply, boosting price performance further.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn only three other occasions have we ever seen Bitcoin withdrawn from exchanges at this rate,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WClementeIII/status/1514253794791641098"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  alongside data from on-chain analytics firm Glassnode.\par \par \uc2 Glassnode's net position change indicator tracks both upwards and downwards changes in balances on 18 exchanges.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-04/537bddd7-ca8a-4283-9bc5-9bc2fa216a03.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Exchange net position change annotated chart. Source: William Clemente/ Twitter\par \par \uc2 Exchange withdrawal spikes are a much-debated phenomenon, and excitement among pundits has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheRealPlanC/status/1511154010518171652"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased}}}\uc2  this year in line with accelerating demand.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author 