24AMP&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $AMP}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/67Pb7xneoQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/67Pb7xneoQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Grayscale (@Grayscale) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Grayscale/status/1478163024934486024?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 4, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 In 2021, cryptocurrency {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-funds-attracted-9-3b-in-inflows-in-2021-as-institutional-adoption-grew"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investment funds generated over $9.3 billion}}}\uc2  in inflows as institutional adoption rose to new highs. Grayscale is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/grayscale-confirms-bitcoin-etf-plans-and-adds-exposure-to-zcash-stellar-lumens-and-horizen-to-its-trusts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gearing up to offer a Bitcoin Spot}}}\uc2  exchange-traded fund (ETF) and said it was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/grayscale-gears-up-for-legal-battle-with-sec-over-bitcoin-etf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 willing to pursue legal action}}}\uc2  if the investment product remains barred by the United States Securities and Exchange (SEC).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDQvMjg3ZmYwMDktNzQ1MC00NWMyLTgxMmMtOWQwZDEwODI4ODY1LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220407ei4700030\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Synthetix\par \b \uc2 Sushi and Synthetix get the boot in Grayscale DeFi fund rebalancing\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Tom Mitchelhill \par \uc2 451 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 April 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Industry leading \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  management firm Grayscale has removed SushiSwap and Synthetix from its DeFi Fund while adding three new tokens to other funds during the firm\u8217\'20\'19s first quarterly rebalancing of this year.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  management firm Grayscale, has added three new cryptocurrency assets across three main investment funds, while removing two other assets from its Decentralized Finance Fund as part of this year\u8217\'20\'19s first quarterly rebalance.\par \par \uc2 Grayscale removed tokens from crypto-derivatives decentralized exchange Synthetix (SNX), and decentralized exchange SushiSwap (SUSHI), from its DeFi fund after the two crypto assets failed to meet the required minimum market capitalization. No other cryptocurrencies were removed during the rebalancing.\par \par \uc2 Grayscale\u8217\'20\'19s DeFi fund, which was launched in July last year, currently holds approximately $8 million in assets. The digital assets remaining in the DeFi fund after the quarterly rebalance include Uniswap (UNI), Aave (AAVE), Curve (CRV), MakerDAO (MKR), Amp (AMP), Yearn Finance (YFI) and Compound (COMP).\par \par \uc2 The crypto asset manager added Avalanche (AVAX) and Polkadot (DOT) to its Digital Large Cap Fund, alongside adding Cosmos (ATOM) to its Smart Contract Platform Ex-Ethereum Fund (GSCPxE Fund).\par \par \uc2 The GSCPxE Fund, which was launched on March 22nd, offers investors the ability to bet on an index of Ethereum\u8217\'20\'19s largest competitors. The GSCPxE Fund\u8217\'20\'19s current holdings listed by the total amount held are \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 , SOL, AVAX, DOT, MATIC, ALGO, XLM and ATOM.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-is-like-the-best-and-worst-parts-of-new-york-grayscale"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum is like the best and worst parts of New York: Grayscale}}}\par \par \uc2 Grayscale remains the world\u8217\'20\'19s leading crypto asset manager, reporting that it held $43.5 billion in assets under management as of Jan. 3rd, this year. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://grayscale.com/products/grayscale-bitcoin-trust/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Grayscale Bitcoin Trust (GBTC)}}}\uc2  remains the largest fund with just over $30 billion in AUM, but has traded at an increasing discount to its net-asset-value for the past year. GBTC is followed in size by the \uc2 Grayscale Ethereum Trust\uc2  (ETCG) which currently holds approximately $11.8 billion in AUM.\par \par \uc2 01/03/22 UPDATE: Net Assets Under Management, Holdings per Share, and Market Price per Share for our Investment Products.\par \par \uc2 Total AUM: $43.5 billion {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BTC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BTC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BAT&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BAT}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BCH&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BCH}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24LINK&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $LINK}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24MANA&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $MANA}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24ETH&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $ETH}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24ETC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $ETC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24FIL&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $FIL}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24ZEN&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $ZEN}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24LTC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $LTC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24LPT&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Et