ht22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  here, after the break of all the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  MS + correctives moves to the upside," Capo {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CryptoCapo_/status/1498390220517093386"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  on March 1, adding:\par \par \uc2 "You can enjoy the LTF pumps while they last, but don't get too comfy."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  outlook lined up with a \uc2 CoinShares{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinshares.com/research/digital-asset-fund-flows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report published last week}}}\uc2  showed most altcoin-based investment vehicles witnessing negative \b \highlight22\uc2 investor sentiment\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ), Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ), and \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-03/a3e7503e-fa74-470c-b675-eb4c1cc68b14.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Flow by asset in the week ending Feb. 25. Source: Bloomberg, \uc2 CoinShares\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-investment-funds-attract-36m-in-capital-despite-market-turmoil"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto investment funds attract $36M in capital despite market turmoil}}}\par \par \uc2 Solana also suffered as the week ending Feb. 25 saw SOL investment products losing $2.6 million in capital outflows.\par \par \uc2 In contrast, all the \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  investment products combined attracted $36 million in the same period, with multi-asset portfolios injecting the highest capital \u8212\'20\'14 of $14 million, followed by Bitcoin's 17.3 million.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph.com. Every investment and trading move involves risk, you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDMvNTQ0Y2JjNjMtOWI2Ny00MmVkLThhODItNWMxODYyZGRkYjNhLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220302ei320005m\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 2/28: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , SOL, AVAX, LUNA, DOGE, DOT\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,728 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 February 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and altcoins surprised investors with a sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  breakout today, signaling a possible change in the short-term trend.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) soared above $40,000 on Feb. 28 even though the S&P 500 remained soft. This suggests that the correlation between Bitcoin and the U.S. equity markets may be showing the first signs of decoupling. If bulls sustain the price above $38,500 till the end of the day, Bitcoin would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/wall-street-open-sends-bitcoin-toward-40k-as-latest-btc-price-surge-nears-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 avoid four successive months of decline}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the past few days does not seem to have shaken the resolve of the long-term investors planning to stick with their positions. Data from on-chain analytics firm Glassnode showed that the amount of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/non-zero-btc-addresses-hit-all-time-high-of-40-million"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin supply that last moved}}}\uc2  between three to five years ago soared to more than 2.8 million Bitcoin, which is a four-year high.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/7d6c7777-85f6-4a03-a501-01edfe2d450a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Interestingly, an experiment by Portuguese software developer Tiago Vasconcelos to develop an artificial intelligence trading bot for Bitcoin resulted in the bot concluding that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe best move is to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/hodl-don-t-trade-says-the-ai-bitcoin-trading-bot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 buy as soon as possible}}}\uc2  and never sell!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Could bulls sustain the momentum and push Bitcoin toward the next overhead resistance? Will altcoins also join the party? Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin turned down from the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) ($40,261) on Feb. 26 but the bears could not pull the price below $37,000. The price rebounded sharply on Feb. 28 and the bulls have cleared the overhead hurdle at the 50-day SMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/2118193a-91e2-4dde-b950-991070b6433b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If bulls sustain the price above the 50-day SMA, the BTC/USDT pair could start its northward journey toward the resistance line of the channel. The bears are expected to mount a strong defense at this level. The bulls will have to push the pair above the channel to indicate that the correction may be over.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($39,813) is flattening out and the relative strength index (RSI) has risen to just above the midpoint. This indicates that the bulls are attempting a strong comeback.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will invalidate in the short term if the price fails to sustain above the moving averages. The pair could then again drop to the support line of the channel.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the 50-day SMA ($2,865) and dropped to the support line of the triangle indicating that higher levels continue to attract selling by the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/e458f610-9a44-4413-a4e0-30d3693a4c3f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price has rebounded off the support line of the triangle but the bulls will have to push and sustain the ETH/USDT pair above the 50-day SMA to signal a possible change in the short-term trend. If that happens, the pair could rally to the resistance line of the triangle.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down from the moving averages, it will suggest that the bears continue to sell at higher levels. That will increase the possibility of a break below the triangle. A close below the triangle could open the doors for a possible retest at $2,300.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  turned down from the 20-day EMA ($385) on Feb. 26 but the price has rebounded sharply off the strong support at $350 on Feb. 28. This indicates that the price is stuck between these two levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/0a95752e-1883-4519-a778-4b41bc761027.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping down and the RSI is just below the midpoint, indicating that bears have a slight edge. If the price turns down from the 20-day EMA, the possibility of a break below $350 increases. If that happens, the BNB/USDT pair could drop to the $330 to $320 support zone.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price rises from the current level and breaks above the moving averages, it will indicate that the bulls are attempting a comeback. The pair could then rally to $445.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the downtrend line on Feb. 26, indicating that bears are defending this resistance with vigor. A minor positive is that the bulls are defending the support at the 50-day SMA ($0.72).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/d8374560-10e2-4159-9aa3-ff5b1b9c49e2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price maintains above $0.75, the bulls will again attempt to push and sustain the XRP/USDT pair above the downtrend line. If they succeed, it could clear the path for a possible rally to $0.91.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns down from the current level, the bears will try to pull the pair below $0.68. If that happens, the pair could retest the Feb. 24 intraday low at $0.62. The flattish moving averages and the RSI just above the midpoint do not give a clear advantage either to the bulls or the bears.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls have sustained Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) above $0.82 in the past few days but are struggling to push the price to the breakdown level at $1. This indicates that demand dries up at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/d0383a42-6b04-43e6-9636-7de55de85201.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The longer the price sustains below the moving averages, the greater the possibility of a retest of the recent intraday low at $0.74. If this support cracks, the downtrend could resume and the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could plunge to $0.68.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price rises and breaks above $1, it will suggest that the markets have rejected the lower levels. The pair could then rise to the resistance line of the descending channel. The bulls will have to push and sustain the price above the channel to indicate that the downtrend may have ended.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana (SOL) has been sandwiched between the 20-day EMA ($94) and the strong support at $81 but this tight range trading is unlikely to continue for long.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/f235e957-3426-4df5-85bf-419e0946c8a1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The RSI is showing signs of forming a positive divergence, signaling that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum may be slowing. If bulls push and sustain the price above the 20-day EMA, the SOL/USDT pair could rise to the resistance line of the descending channel.\par \par \uc2 A break and close above the channel will be the first indication that the bears may be losing their grip. The pair could then rise to the overhead resistance at $122. This positive view will invalidate on a break and close below $81.\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT\par \par \uc2 Avalanche ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ) has been oscillating near the moving averages for the past three days. Although bulls pushed the price above the moving averages on Feb. 25, they could not sustain the higher levels. Strong selling pulled the price back below the moving averages on Feb. 27.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/dd1ecec2-f4b6-40d6-a8c0-d93ab08b4e3a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls are currently attempting to sustain the price above the moving averages. If they manage to do that, the AVAX/USDT pair could rally to the downtrend line of the descending channel. This level could act as a stiff resistance but if bulls overcome it, the pair will indicate that the downtrend may have ended.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the current level or the overhead resistance, it will suggest that bears continue to sell on rallies. The bears could gain strength if the price slips below $64.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ebay-to-add-crypto-payment-options-soon-says-ceo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eBay to add crypto payment options soon, says CEO}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT\par \par \uc2 Terra\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/terra-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LUNA}}}\uc2  token turned down from $80 but the bulls successfully defended the immediate support at $70. This indicates that traders are accumulating on every minor dip.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/064686cc-fb1b-4826-903d-102db1ef1af1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The buying picked up momentum on Feb. 28 and the bulls pushed the price above the overhead resistance at $70. The upsloping 20-day EMA ($62) and the RSI in the overbought territory indicate that bulls are in control.\par \par \uc2 The LUNA/USDT pair could now rise to $90 where the bears may again mount a strong resistance. A break and close above this level could propel the pair to the all-time high at $103.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down from $90, the pair could again drop to $70 and consolidate between these two levels for a few days.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) has been struggling to bounce off the strong support at $0.12, indicating a lack of urgency among bulls to buy at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/d54c75eb-0a77-4fc0-b6c2-4e88ac15fac0.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The longer the price clings to the strong support at $0.12 without a strong bounce, the greater the possibility of a breakdown. If the bears pull the price below $0.12, the DOGE/USDT pair could retest the psychological support at $0.10.\par \par \uc2 This is an important level for the bulls to defend because if it cracks, the selling could intensify further and the pair could slide to $0.06. The first sign of strength will be a break and close above the 50-day SMA ($0.14). That could result in a rally to $0.17.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot\u8217\'20\'19s (DOT) recovery stalled at the downtrend line, indicating that the sentiment remains negative and traders are selling on rallies to strong resistance levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/fb0a8274-5da5-49e2-a008-f47e1ff35406.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price could remain stuck between the downtrend line and $14 for the next few days. If bears pull the price below $14, the DOT/USDT pair could resume its downtrend and decline to the strong support at $10.\par \par \uc2 The buyers will have to push and sustain the price above the downtrend line to signal that the bears may be losing their grip. The pair could then rally to the overhead resistance at $23 where the bears may mount a strong defense.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDIvMWI4MDcxYmYtNTRiOS00MTQ2LTlhZmMtZDAzYzdjZTU1OTVkLkpQRw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220228ei2s000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Bitcoin consolidates after $40K surge as analyst eyes weekly higher low for BTC price\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By William Suberg \par \uc2 450 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 February 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 BTC price action stays above the January low as Bitcoin sees a snap return to $40,000.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) began a nervous weekend at around $39,000 on Feb. 26 after an overnight spike briefly saw $40,000 return.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/e1fceb25-0655-492a-b64c-5c0da8fcf4f2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD 1-hour candle chart (\uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 ). Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Stocks gains but crypto "fear" pervades\par \par \uc2 Data from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.cointelegraph.com/?via=markets&_ga=2.142027444.742658523.1640948929-762064149.1640948929"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cointelegraph Markets Pro}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSD/?exchange=BINANCE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\uc2  revealed calmer conditions for BTC/USD Saturday after overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw highs of $40,330 on \uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 With traditional markets closed, the probability of "fakeout" moves up or down was elevated thanks to thinner weekend volumes on crypto markets.\par \par \uc2 The geopolitical turmoil focused on Ukraine and occupier Russia formed the backdrop for continued cautious sentiment, amid concerns that Monday, in particular, could bring fresh instability.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://alternative.me/crypto/fear-and-greed-index/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto Fear & Greed Index}}}\uc2 , while inching up towards the end of the week, remained in the low "fear" zone at 26/100.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/a1fd1584-7888-40a5-a6c0-d640cf4c3808.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto Fear & Greed Index (screenshot). Source: Alternative.me\par \par \uc2 A potential silver lining for Bitcoin bulls meanwhile came from the weekly chart. With its recent $34,300 low on the Ukraine invasion, BTC nonetheless managed to put in a higher low versus January's $32,800 dip.\par \par \uc2 Should that hold, trader and analyst Rekt Capital believed, February's comedown from $45,500 would most likely turn out to have been a "necessary" consolidation move.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BTC?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BTC}}}\par \par \uc2 Mission Accomplished {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BTC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BTC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Crypto?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Crypto}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Bitcoin?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Bitcoin}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IYHnRJFDlu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IYHnRJFDlu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rekt Capital (@rektcapital) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rektcapital/status/1497222581786759175?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Macro markets meanwhile ended the week on a high, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-whales-fuel-btc-price-comeback-as-stocks-brush-off-russia-ukraine-shocks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significant rebounds}}}\uc2  for both European and U.S. indices.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar, which had surged in strength as hostilities began, gave back most of its gains, with the U.S. dollar currency index (DXY) returning to 96.5 from highs of 97.7.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/a28caf52-c14d-42bd-98be-33734fc5a3e7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 U.S. dollar currency index (DXY) 1-hour candle chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 LUNA leads top ten altcoins higher\par \par \uc2 Altcoins provided a mixed but still overall strong picture Saturday, major tokens led by Terra ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/terra-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LUNA}}}\uc2  ), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/terra-luna-price-nears-key-level-after-rallying-45-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 up almost 50% in a week}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/price-analysis-2-25-btc-eth-bnb-xrp-ada-sol-avax-luna-doge-dot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 2/25: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , SOL, AVAX, LUNA, DOGE, DOT}}}\par \par \uc2 With Bitcoin cooling, some late gains were still playing out, including for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2 , which was 10.3% higher over the 24 hours to the time of writing.\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ), the largest altcoin by market cap, traded above $2,750 on the back of 5.6% daily gains, having sought to challenge $2,900 overnight.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/4172520d-ea9c-4ac4-aa4f-fb11c0a9aef7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD 1-hour candle chart (\uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 ). Source: TradingView\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDIvZTVjMTFjOTYtNTljNS00ZDFhLTlkODctZTdiODM1OWJmODc3LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220226ei2q0002t\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Terra\par \b \uc2 Terra LUNA price nears key level after rallying 45% this week\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Yashu Gola \par \uc2 455 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 February 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 LUNA has outperformed almost every top-ranking cryptocurrency this week despite dampening risk-on sentiments.\par \par \uc2 A rebound rally in the Terra ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/terra-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LUNA}}}\uc2  ) market this week risks exhaustion as the price retests a key trendline for a potential pullback.\par \par \uc2 Descending channel risks LUNA decline\par \par \uc2 LUNA has been trending lower inside a falling channel\u8212\'20\'14made up of two parallel descending trendlines\u8212\'20\'14since December 2021. In doing so, the Terra token typically tests the lower trendline as support for a rebound to the upper trendline, as shown in the chart below.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/e162975f-1748-4c6f-b75a-b8dad837fa6e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USD daily price chart featuring falling channel. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Similarly, a pullback from the upper trendline sends the price to the lower trendline. For now, LUNA looks poised to repeat the correction move, taking further cues from its daily relative strength index that now treads near its overbought reading of 70 \u8212\'20\'14 a sell indicator.\par \par \uc2 If the pullback occurs, the price would risk dropping to its interim downside target near $52, coinciding with the 0.5 Fib line of the Fibonacci retracement graph drawn from $4-swing low to $100-swing high.\par \par \uc2 If an extended correction occurs, LUNA could retest $40, a 0.618 Fib line that comes closest to the falling channel's lower trendline.\par \par \uc2 LUNA best performer this week so far\par \par \uc2 The short-term \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  outlook appears after Terra's 45% price rally to around $68 this week, its best level since Jan. 25. Interestingly, LUNA/USD went higher despite a gloomy outlook elsewhere in the crypto market, led by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-whales-fuel-btc-price-comeback-as-stocks-brush-off-russia-ukraine-shocks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russian military's invasion of Ukraine}}}\uc2  that dampened investors' risk-on sentiments.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/terra-avoids-ukraine-concerns-rallying-18-in-three-days-can-luna-price-reach-200-next"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Terra avoids Ukraine concerns rallying 18% in three days \u8212\'20\'14 Can LUNA price reach $200 next?}}}\par \par \uc2 The next-best performing token this week among the top cryptos has been Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ). Interestingly, \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 's week-to-date returns sit near 6% below zero, meaning LUNA has been outperforming its nearest rivals, including Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) and Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ), by a wide percentage margin in the said period.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/8bca51d8-3fd1-4797-aa85-ebc62944098c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA weekly performance vs. other top assets. Source: Messari\par \par \uc2 LUNA's superior performance appeared partly due to the news surrounding the $1 billion {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/luna-foundation-guard-raises-1b-to-form-ust-reserve-denominated-in-bitcoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raised}}}\uc2  to establish a Bitcoin reserve for Terra's stablecoin UST. Additionally, Anchor Protocol (ANC), which recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/terra-injects-450m-ust-into-anchor-reserve-days-before-protocol-depletion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received a $450 million UST}}}\uc2  from the Luna Foundation Guard (LFG), rose by nearly 70% under Terra's shadow.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph.com. Every investment and trading move involves risk, you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDIvYmJjZTEzZWQtNzBiYi00YTJmLWE1ZmYtY2YwOGMwMTljNTU4LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220225ei2p000ba\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 CoinShares\par \b \uc2 $89M flows into Bitcoin funds despite looming conflict, but ETH funds are negative\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Brian Quarmby \par \uc2 386 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 February 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Institutional investors snapped up $89 million worth of BTC investment products last week, while Ether products saw outflows totaling $15.2 million.\par \par \uc2 Amid a marketwide downturn across major crypto assets over the past week, institutional traders tipped almost $89 million into Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) funds. However, the money men failed to back Ethereum ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) investment products, which saw outflows totaling $15.2 million.\par \par \uc2 Despite Cointelegraph reporting earlier this week that activity on the Bitcoin network was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-network-activity-down-30-from-highs-as-tepid-demand-mimics-mid-2019"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 down 30% since its ATH}}}\uc2  levels three months ago, digital gold appears to be the asset of choice for sophisticated investors of late.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 Tuesday \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Digital Asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund Flows Weekly\u8221\'20\'1D report, BTC funds have now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/coinshares/volume-67-digital-asset-fund-flows-weekly-report-2aab8cae9950"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pulled}}}\uc2  in a total of $178.3 million this month following the latest $89 million influx between Feb. 14 and Friday.\par \par \uc2 In comparison, Ether investment products have seen total outflows of $2.6 million in February so far, and have only generated inflows in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ether-investment-products-register-first-weekly-inflows-in-10-weeks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of the past 11 weeks}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Over the past seven days, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/analysts-say-bitcoin-bottom-is-in-as-btc-bounces-back-to-38-000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 price of BTC has dipped}}}\uc2  14.6% to sit at roughly $38,000, while Ether has dropped 16.2% to $2,668 at the time of writing. Other top assets such as Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) and Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) have also suffered double-digit losses.\par \par \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  noted that despite \u8220\'20\'1Cprice weakness and perceived negative impact from the looming conflict in Eastern Europe,\u8221\'20\'1D \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  investment products in general saw inflows totaling $109 last week.\par \par \uc2 Outside of Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s dominance, institutional traders also snapped up $25 million worth of investment products tied to Ethereum competitor Avalanche, while multi-asset and Solana funds also saw notable inflows of $9.4 million and $1.2 million each.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFollowing the run of outflows in January, the latest data marks the 5th week of inflows. While inflows were seen in both Europe and the Americas, it was predominantly the latter with inflows totaling US$101M."\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-could-probe-lower-as-volumes-dip-and-macroeconomic-issues-loom-overhead"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin price could \u8216\'20\'18probe lower\u8217\'20\'19 as volumes dip and macroeconomic issues loom overhead}}}\par \par \uc2 In terms of the institutional asset managers and fund providers, \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  XBT fund shed $21.6 million, while Purpose and ProShares saw inflows of $63.2 million and $26.6 million, respectively.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDIvYzM0YTFjM2QtYTQ0ZC00Yjg4LTk3ZjgtNzkyYmRmYTVhZmQ2LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220223ei2n000ba\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 2/23: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , SOL, AVAX, LUNA, DOGE, DOT\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,796 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 February 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 BTC and altcoins flashed a few \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  signals today, but traders say $38,000 is still the level Bitcoin needs to close above before a reversal can begin.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) and several altcoins have bounced off their immediate support levels after buyers attempted to arrest the current decline. Bloomberg Senior Commodity Strategist Mike McGlone highlighted in a recent Tweet that Bitcoin was trading roughly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-could-probe-lower-as-volumes-dip-and-macroeconomic-issues-loom-overhead"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 20% below its 50-week moving average}}}\uc2  and such discounted levels have \u8220\'20\'1Coften resulted in good price support.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  price action of the past few days does not seem to have deterred the institutional traders from accumulating at lower levels. According to \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 Feb. 22 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Digital Asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund Flows Weekly\u8221\'20\'1D report, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/89m-flows-into-bitcoin-funds-despite-looming-conflict-but-eth-funds-are-negative"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 institutional investors pumped about $89 million}}}\uc2  into Bitcoin funds between Feb. 14 and Feb. 18, taking the total inflows in the current month to $178.3 million.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/142a021d-1526-4c51-9d87-c6ab38ecf52e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto traders do not seem to be too scared by the current 50% correction. In a survey conducted by \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 , only about 35% of the respondents said they would reduce their trading in an extremely \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crypto market condition. A majority, more than 70%, said they planned to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/deep-bullishness-for-crypto-analyst-comments-on-deutsche-bank-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increase their crypto activity}}}\uc2  over the next six months.\par \par \uc2 Could Bitcoin and altcoins sustain the relief rally or will bears pounce and stall the recovery? Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin bounced from the first support at $36,250 and the bulls will now attempt to push the price above the overhead resistance zone between $39,600 and the 50-day simple moving average ($40,615).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/0c67ad89-dac5-499e-8f26-fe6b0d870fed.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they manage to do that, the BTC/USDT pair could rise to $45,821 where the bears are likely to mount a stiff resistance.\par \par \uc2 The long wick on today\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick suggests that bears are attempting to flip $39,600 into resistance. The downsloping moving averages and the relative strength index in the negative territory suggest that bears have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 A break and close below $36,250 will signal the resumption of the down move. The pair could then decline to $34,000 and later retest the Jan. 24 low at $32,917.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) bounced off the psychological support at $2,500 on Feb. 22. The bulls have pushed the price above the breakdown level of $2,652, indicating strong buying at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/c2559a51-1879-440f-8e1d-8e3cd662ca19.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The buyers will now try to propel the price above the moving averages. If they succeed, the ETH/USDT pair could rally to the resistance line of the symmetrical triangle pattern. The bulls will have to push the price above the triangle to signal the start of a new uptrend.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns down from the moving averages, the bears will try to pull the pair below the support line of the triangle. If they manage to do that, it will suggest that the symmetrical triangle has acted as a continuation pattern. The pair could then drop to $2,159 and later to $2,000.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) bounced off the strong support at $350 on Feb. 22 indicating that bulls have not given up and they continue to buy at lower levels. The bulls will now attempt to drive the price above the downtrend line of the descending channel.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/77b1b12e-3487-4735-bdb0-0c99f2997c7f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they manage to do that, the BNB/USDT pair could rise to the 50-day SMA ($416). This is an important level for the bears to defend because a break above it could signal a possible change in trend. The pair could thereafter rise to $445.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down from the downtrend line, the bears will fancy their chances and make one more attempt to pull the pair below $350. If that happens, the pair could drop to the strong support zone at $330 to $320.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/ripple"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) bounced off $0.66 on Feb. 2 and the bulls pushed the price above the 50-day SMA ($0.72). The buyers will now attempt to clear the overhead hurdle at $0.75.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/4530d68a-a711-48d8-a70b-d801ffeb156c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they manage to do that, the XRP/USDT pair could rise to the downtrend line. The bulls will have to push the pair above this line to indicate that bulls are back in the game. The pair could then rally to $0.91.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns down from $0.75, it will suggest that bears have flipped the level into resistance. The bears will then attempt to pull the price below $0.66 and extend the decline to $0.60.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) has bounced off the strong support near $0.80, indicating that buyers are attempting to arrest the decline. The price could now reach the breakdown level at $1.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/683bb2e9-19b2-47b8-a640-d1e77e79417d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If buyers push and sustain the price above $1, it will suggest that the markets have rejected the lower levels. The bulls will then attempt to push the price to the resistance line of the descending channel. A break and close above the channel will signal a possible trend change.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from $1, it will suggest that bears have flipped this level into resistance. The sellers will then try to pull the pair below $0.80 and resume the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/solana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) bounced off the $81 support on Feb. 22, indicating that buyers are attempting to defend this level. The RSI is showing signs of forming a positive divergence, indicating that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum could be weakening.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/475ccd9d-f5c7-4024-9a53-65bb0701d8ec.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If buyers drive and sustain the price above the 20-day EMA ($97), the SOL/USDT pair could rally to the resistance line of the descending channel. This level could act as a major barrier but if bulls overcome it, the pair could rally to $122.\par \par \uc2 A break and close above this resistance will complete a double bottom pattern. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup has a target objective at $163. This positive view will invalidate if the price turns down from the 20-day EMA or the resistance line and plummets below $81. That could open the doors for a further decline to $66.\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT\par \par \uc2 Avalanche ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/avalanche"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ) broke below the moving averages on Feb. 20 but the bears could not build upon this advantage. Strong buying near $67 has resulted in a rebound and the price has reached the moving averages.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/d8acaae8-2c60-42a4-9915-9750690ad237.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If buyers push and sustain the price above the moving averages, the AVAX/USDT pair could rally to the downtrend line. The bears are likely to defend this level aggressively.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the downtrend line but bounces off the moving averages, it will indicate that traders are buying on dips. That will improve the prospects of a break above the channel. If that happens, the pair could first rise to $100 and then rally toward $117.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down from the current level, the bears will attempt to pull the pair below $67 and resume the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/even-in-a-choppy-crypto-market-this-algorithmic-indicator-helped-traders-identify-the-few-winners"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Even in a choppy crypto market, this algorithmic indicator helped traders identify the few winners}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT\par \par \uc2 Terra\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/terra-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LUNA}}}\uc2  token broke and closed above the 20-day EMA ($54) on Feb. 22 which was the first indication that the sellers may be losing their grip. Sustained buying has pushed the price to the downtrend line of the descending channel.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/35db7b81-9721-4cdf-b948-c3ee9ea21493.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the RSI has jumped into the positive territory, suggesting a minor advantage to buyers. A break and close above the 50-day SMA ($62) will indicate a possible trend change. The LUNA/USDT pair could then rally to $70 where it may again face resistance from the bears.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the 50-day SMA, it will signal that bears are attempting to defend the overhead resistance. If the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA, it will indicate that bulls are buying the dips. That will increase the possibility of a break above the 50-day SMA. This positive view will be negated if bears pull the price below the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/dogecoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) rebounded off the strong support at $0.12 on Feb. 12, suggesting that the bulls have not yet given up and are buying on dips.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/b1bb2196-3e0b-4a92-ab4b-acbda3042d54.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The relief rally is likely to face strong resistance at the moving averages but the positive divergence on the RSI favors the buyers. If the bulls push and sustain the price above the 50-day SMA ($0.14), the DOGE/USDT pair could rise to $0.17.\par \par \uc2 A break and close above this level will complete a double bottom pattern, which has a target objective at $0.22. Conversely, if the price turns down from the moving averages, the bears will fancy their chances and try to sink the pair below $0.12. If they succeed, the pair could drop to $0.10.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) has bounced off the support at $15.80, indicating that the bulls have not given up and they continue to buy at lower levels. The RSI is showing signs of forming a positive divergence, suggesting that the selling momentum could be weakening.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/7dbfae1d-442e-40a6-a08c-1230577bd02b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The DOT/USDT pair could now rise to the downtrend line, which is likely to act as a strong resistance. If the price turns down from this level, the bears will again attempt to pull the pair below $15.80 and resume the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if bulls drive the price above the downtrend line and the 50-day SMA ($21.14), the pair could rise to the overhead resistance at $23.19. A break and close above this level will complete a double bottom pattern.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDIvZjlhN2JkMGYtNTFhNy00ZGRmLWJmNTMtZmVmNzYxOTdkMjY5LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220223ei2n000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Bitcoin traders mark levels to watch as BTC price bounces to $39K\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By William Suberg \par \uc2 523 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 February 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 BTC price action returns to $39,000 amid warnings of "heavy resistance" for Bitcoin coming up.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) began to see much-welcomed \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the upside on Feb. 23 as European markets opened with modest upside.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/f17eb9f6-0995-4e72-83b2-5eabd198b797.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD 1-hour candle chart (\uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 ). Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 $39,600 set to spark "heavy resistance"\par \par \uc2 Data from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.cointelegraph.com/?via=markets&_ga=2.142027444.742658523.1640948929-762064149.1640948929"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cointelegraph Markets Pro}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSD/?exchange=BINANCE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\uc2  showed BTC/USD rapidly gaining Wednesday, hitting $39,000 before consolidating.\par \par \uc2 The pair had staged a steady comeback overnight, with progress totalling 6.8% versus {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-dips-to-36-4k-as-ukraine-move-sends-russian-ruble-to-near-6-year-lows-vs-dollar"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tuesday's lows}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Seems I'm not getting that little pull back but continuation higher already. Doesn't change the structure really much. $40k is key level," popular trader Crypto Ed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Crypto_Ed_NL/status/1496402682000596993"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reacted}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Crypto_Ed_NL/status/1496402682000596993/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://twitter.com/Crypto_Ed_NL/status/1496402682000596993/photo/1}}}\par \par \uc2 Previously, Crypto Ed had warned that any push towards the $40,000 could well end up as a relief bounce followed by an even deeper correction than that seen this week.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MatthewHyland_/status/1496363973905637380/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Summarizing}}}\uc2  the short-term scenario, meanwhile, fellow trader and analyst Matthew Hyland presented $36,300 and $33,000 as the support levels in play. For him, $39,600 was once again the upside resistance zone to clear, as it had been earlier in February.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/c9bbfc8a-e71d-44e6-9c53-d07c7781a69f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD annotated chart. Source: Matthew Hyland/ Twitter\par \par \uc2 "Expect heavy resistance and likely rejection in the 39.5-40k area if we get there," \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account Cheds {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BigCheds/status/1496277039476883459"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After Tuesday's lows entered, analytics tool Material Indicators had meanwhile eyed an uptick in buyer behavior after days of indecision.\par \par \uc2 Market buyers finally got off their hands and started pushing the green button. Marked up another FireChart to help you interpret the intraday moves. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BTC?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BTC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Datavisualization?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Datavisualization}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Crypto?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Crypto}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/tradingstrategy?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #tradingstrategy}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zw0ufgPIMt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/zw0ufgPIMt}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rrpBB05vS2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rrpBB05vS2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Material Indicators (@MI_Algos) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MI_Algos/status/1496168435759427584?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Market buyers finally got off their hands and started pushing the green button," it announced on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  alongside a chart showing increasing order volumes of both large and small buys.\par \par \uc2 A look at order book data from major exchange Binance on Wednesday meanwhile showed BTC/USD beginning to tackle a band of resistance with its latest move higher.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/d6133b88-3833-41b2-88ac-c81fa38c9d39.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Binance order book data chart. Source: Material Indicators\par \par \uc2 Altcoins bounce back with 'altseason' talk in the air\par \par \uc2 A good day was being had by altcoins on Wednesday, with major tokens beating Bitcoin's own solid 24-hour performance.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/you-d-better-buy-some-bitcoin-btc-figures-defy-canada-gov-t-as-etf-assets-hit-record"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 'You'd better buy some Bitcoin' \u8212\'20\'14 BTC figures defy Canada gov't as ETF assets hit record}}}\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) was up 6.1% to $2,700 at the time of writing, indicative of many of the top-ten cryptocurrencies by market cap.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/cc69653b-7a90-4e7e-aa0a-74e8ceb008bd.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD 1-hour candle chart (\uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 ). Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The list was led by another solid run from Terra ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/terra-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LUNA}}}\uc2  ), which gained 14% over the same period, followed by Avalanche ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ) on 11.8% and Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) on 9.7%.\par \par \uc2 Talk of an upcoming "altseason," meanwhile, also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BTCfuel/status/1496110661855854597"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remained popular}}}\uc2  on social media.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDIvZjE3MGFlYWItNDg3Yy00MDhkLTk5OGItNmM1MGEzODFmZWY4LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220223ei2n0002v\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 CoinShares\par \b \uc2 $89M flows into Bitcoin funds despite looming conflict, but ETH funds are negative\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Brian Quarmby \par \uc2 390 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 February 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Institutional investors snapped up $89 million worth of BTC investment products last week, while Ether products saw outflows totaling $15.2 million.\par \par \uc2 Amid a marketwide downturn across major crypto assets over the past week, institutional traders tipped almost $89 million into Bitcoin (BTC) funds. However, the money men failed to ba Ethereum (ETH) investment products, which saw outflows totaling $15.2 million.\par \par \uc2 Despite Cointelegraph reporting earlier this week that activity on the Bitcoin network was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-network-activity-down-30-from-highs-as-tepid-demand-mimics-mid-2019"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 down 30% since its ATH}}}\uc2  levels three months ago, digital gold appears to be the asset of choice for sophisticated investors of late.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 Feb. 22 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Digital Asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund Flows Weekly\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/coinshares/volume-67-digital-asset-fund-flows-weekly-report-2aab8cae9950"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2 , BTC funds have now pulled in a total of $178.3 million this month following the latest $89 million influx between Feb. 14 and Feb. 18.\par \par \uc2 In comparison, Ether investment products offering have now seen total outflows of $2.6 million in February so far, and have only generated inflows in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ether-investment-products-register-first-weekly-inflows-in-10-weeks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of the past 11 weeks}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Over the past seven days, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/analysts-say-bitcoin-bottom-is-in-as-btc-bounces-back-to-38-000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 price of BTC has dipped}}}\uc2  14.6% to sit at roughly $38,000, while Ether has dropped 16.2% to $2,668 at the time of writing. Other top assets such as Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), Solana (SOL) and Ripple (XRP) have also suffered double-digit losses.\par \par \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  noted that despite \u8220\'20\'1Cprice weakness and perceived negative impact from the looming conflict in Eastern Europe,\u8221\'20\'1D \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  investment products in general saw inflows totaling $109 last week.\par \par \uc2 Outside of Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s dominance, institutional traders also snapped up $25 million worth of investment products tied to Ethereum competitor Avalanche, while multi-asset and Solana funds also saw notable inflows of $9.4 million and $1.2 million each.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFollowing the run of outflows in January, the latest data marks the 5th week of inflows. While inflows were seen in both Europe and the Americas, it was predominantly the latter with inflows totaling US$101M."\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-could-probe-lower-as-volumes-dip-and-macroeconomic-issues-loom-overhead"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin price could \u8216\'20\'18probe lower\u8217\'20\'19 as volumes dip and macroeconomic issues loom overhead}}}\par \par \uc2 In terms of the institutional asset managers and fund providers, \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  XBT fund shed $21.6 million, while Purpose and ProShares saw inflows of $63.2 million and $26.6 million respectively.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDIvYzM0YTFjM2QtYTQ0ZC00Yjg4LTk3ZjgtNzkyYmRmYTVhZmQ2LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220223ei2n00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 2/21: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , SOL, AVAX, LUNA, DOGE, DOT\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,765 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 February 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 BTC\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to reclaim $40,000 was thwarted by bears, but any consolidation within the current range could benefit small and large-cap altcoins.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) dipped below $38,000 on Feb. 21 but the bulls are attempting to arrest the decline and start a recovery. The sustained weakness in 2022 seems to have toned down expectations of a strong rally.\par \par \uc2 Huobi crypto exchange co-founder Du Jun said that if the Bitcoin halving cycle repeats, then the current weakness could be the start of a bear market. Jun believes that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-winter-2022-here-s-what-crypto-industry-veterans-expect"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 next Bitcoin bull cycle is expected}}}\uc2  to begin either at the end of 2024 or at the beginning of 2025.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/78761358-2c8c-47c2-a7cc-b640d370cda4.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 In the short term, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/coin-days-destroyed-spike-hinting-at-btc-price-bottom-5-things-to-watch-in-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crypto markets are likely to be influenced}}}\uc2  by the geopolitical developments between Russia and Ukraine, cues from the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  on its tightening cycle and the performance of the assets perceived as risky.\par \par \uc2 Could Bitcoin and select altcoins recover from the recent lows or will the selling pick up momentum? Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin plunged and closed below the key support at $39,600 on Feb. 20. The selling resumed on Feb. 21 and the bears pulled the price to $37,213.63.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/67a81802-8b02-4d13-8767-6e112b42a41f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The sharp selling in the past few days has pulled the relative strength index (RSI) into the negative territory and the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($40,986) has turned down. This indicates the path of least resistance is to the downside.\par \par \uc2 The buyers are attempting to push the price back above the breakdown level at $39,600. This is an important level to watch out for because if bears flip this level into resistance, the selling could intensify and the BTC/USDT pair could drop to the $36,250 to $35,507.01 support zone.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if bulls push and sustain the price above $39,600 and the moving averages, it will indicate strong demand at lower levels. That could open the gates for a possible rally to $45,821.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) re-entered the descending channel on Feb. 18. This was the first indication that the recovery was faltering. The bulls tried to push the price back above the channel on Feb. 19 but the bears kept up the pressure.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/07a137ba-218c-445e-9976-d1e9fa248083.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The ETH/USDT pair broke and closed below the critical support at $2,652 on Feb. 20 but the sellers could not build upon this advantage. This indicates strong buying at lower levels. The price rebounded sharply on Feb. 21 and the buyers are trying to push the pair above the resistance line of the channel.\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the pair could challenge the moving averages. A break and close above the 50-day simple moving average (SMA)($2,971) could be the first sign of strength.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down from the current level and plummets below $2,652, the pair may slide to $2,316 and then $2,159.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls tried to push Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) back above the downtrend line of the descending channel on Feb. 19 but the bears did not relent.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/7b3b5641-d4d4-44ed-9a42-eea77823bbc3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The selling renewed on Feb. 20 and the bears pulled the price below the strong support at $390.50. This could have triggered stops of traders who may have purchased the break and close above the channel. The long wick on Feb. 21\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick indicates that bears are trying to flip the $390.50 level into resistance.\par \par \uc2 If bears pull the price below $357.40, the BNB/USDT pair could drop to the strong support zone at $330 to $320. The bulls will have to push and sustain the price above the 50-day SMA ($422) to indicate that the bears may be losing their grip.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/ripple"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) bounced off the $0.75 support on Feb. 18 but the relief rally again faltered near the overhead resistance at $0.85 on Feb. 19. This indicates that bears are defending this level aggressively.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/e0900047-bcb0-420a-b52d-4d02fea5b53f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Renewed selling on Feb. 20 has pulled the price to the strong support zone between the moving averages. If this support zone cracks, several stops may be hit and the XRP/USDT pair could slide to $0.65 and later to $0.60.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price rebounds off the support zone, the bulls will attempt to push the pair above the downtrend line and the overhead resistance at $0.85. If they manage to do that, the pair could rally to the psychological level at $1.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) broke and closed below the psychological level at $1 on Feb. 18. This suggests the resumption of the downtrend. The bulls pushed the price back above $1 on Feb. 19 but failed to sustain the higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/1e73eb58-850b-416f-b93d-acf7ac2fcc8f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The long wick on Feb. 21\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick indicates that bears continue to defend the $1 level and are trying to flip it into resistance. If the price sustains below $1, the selling could pick up and the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could decline to the next strong support at $0.80.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns up from the current level and rises above the 50-day SMA ($1.15), it will indicate that markets have rejected the lower levels. That could act as a bear trap, resulting in a possible short squeeze. The pair could then rally to $1.60.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) formed a long-legged Doji candlestick pattern on Feb. 20, indicating indecision among the bulls and bears. The bulls attempted to resolve the uncertainty to the upside on Feb. 21 but the bears successfully defended the 20-day EMA ($100).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/fa04e829-2261-48df-be0d-99417720b407.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping down and the RSI is trading below 38, indicating that bears have the upper hand. The sellers will now attempt to sink the SOL/USDT pair below the strong support at $80.83.\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the pair could resume its downtrend. The next support on the downside is at $66. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will invalidate in the short term if the price breaks and sustains above the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 The bulls will then try to push the pair above the resistance line of the channel and signal a possible trend change.\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT\par \par \uc2 Avalanche ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ) plummeted below the moving averages and the uptrend line on Feb. 20, suggesting that the higher levels continue to attract selling by the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/c3ec9a09-5a41-435d-81a7-0ffcc598557a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls tried to push the price back above the uptrend line on Feb. 2 but the long wick on the candlestick suggests that bears are defending the breakdown level. If the price breaks and sustains below $74.70, the AVAX/USDT pair could further slip to $65.\par \par \uc2 The RSI has dipped into the negative zone and the 20-day EMA ($82) has started to turn down, indicating that bears have the upper hand. This negative view will invalidate if the price rebounds off the current level and breaks above the downtrend line. That could result in a rally to the psychological level at $100.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/solana-s-weekend-bounce-risks-turning-into-a-bull-trap-can-sol-price-fall-to-60-next"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Solana's weekend bounce risks turning into a bull trap \u8212\'20\'14 Can SOL price fall to $60 next?}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT\par \par \uc2 The long tail on the Feb. 20 candlestick indicates that buyers are defending the immediate support at $46.50. Terra\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/terra-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LUNA}}}\uc2  token could now rise to the 20-day EMA ($54) where the bears are expected to mount a strong defense.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/e033c7f1-3c82-4d0b-9034-ce6abbea2d2b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price once again turns down from the 20-day EMA, the prospects of a break below the strong support zone at $46.50 to $43.44 increase. That could sink the LUNA/USDT pair to the critical support at $37.50.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if bulls push and sustain the price above the 20-day EMA, the pair could rise to the downtrend line of the descending channel. The bulls will have to push and sustain the pair above the 50-day SMA ($63) to indicate a possible change in trend.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) attempted to rise above the 20-day EMA ($0.14) on Feb. 19 but the long wick on the candlestick suggests that bears are defending this resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/875fd791-bc12-4535-a2a9-a439a3a08eed.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are sloping down and the RSI is in the negative zone, indicating that bears have the upper hand. The longer the price sustains below the moving averages, the greater the likelihood of a drop to the strong support at $0.12.\par \par \uc2 The bulls are expected to defend this level aggressively because a break below it could result in a decline to the psychological support at $0.10.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will invalidate in the short term if the price turns up and rises above the 50-day SMA ($0.15). That could push the DOGE/USDT pair to $0.17.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) failure to rebound off the strong support at $16.81 indicates a lack of demand at higher levels. This increases the possibility of a further slide.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/bcee5813-740b-4b27-b322-82f16c9cfe1b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If bears pull and sustain the price below $16.81, the selling could accelerate and the DOT/USDT pair could drop to $13 and later retest the critical support at $10.37. The downsloping moving averages and the RSI below 37 indicate the path of least resistance is to the downside.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of strength will be a break and close above the downtrend line. Such a move could open the doors for a possible up-move to the 50-day SMA ($21.67) and later to $23.19.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDIvMzQ0M2VjNDUtMTNkZC00ZGI2LTk3ZDQtMTdhMjZjYmI5NTlkLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220221ei2l000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Morgan Stanley\par \b \uc2 Ethereum dominance may dwindle as competitors emerge: \uc2 Morgan Stanley\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Brian Quarmby \par \uc2 462 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 February 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  has argued that Ether is a riskier investment choice than BTC as Ethereum faces larger competition and scalability issues than Bitcoin.\par \par \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s wealth management global investment office has published a report on Ethereum ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) arguing that the blockchain\u8217\'20\'19s dominance could dwindle if strong market competition emerges.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/morgan-stanley-increased-exposure-to-bitcoin-held-300m-in-grayscale-shares"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investment banking giant\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  report is titled \u8220\'20\'1CCryptocurrency 201: What Is Ethereum?\u8221\'20\'1D and it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://advisor.morganstanley.com/daron.edwards/documents/field/d/da/daron-edwards/Cryptocurrency_201__What_is_Ethereum_.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provides}}}\uc2  a detailed rundown of the ecosystem along with its advantages and disadvantages in relation to Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDue in part to its more ambitious addressable market, Ethereum faces more competitive threats, scalability issues, and complexity challenges than Bitcoin. Furthermore, Ether is more volatile than Bitcoin,\u8221\'20\'1D the report reads.\par \par \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  argued that Ethereum may lose smart contract superiority to cheaper and faster blockchains \u8212\'20\'14 something that has often been argued by supporters of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-killers-or-just-pretenders-ethereum-remains-king-for-now"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum killer}}}\uc2  market that includes networks such as Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), Solana (SOL), Polkadot (DOT), and Tezos (XTZ):\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEthereum faces more competition in the smart contract market than Bitcoin faces in the store-of-value market. Ethereum may lose smart contract platform market share to faster or cheaper alternatives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The investment bank also suggested that Ethereum poses a greater investment risk than Bitcoin as it faces greater competition in the smart contract market than \u8220\'20\'1CBitcoin faces in the store-of-value market.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFewer transactions per user are needed to \u8216\'20\'18use\u8217\'20\'19 Bitcoin, which is akin to a decentralized savings account. Ethereum demand is tied more closely to transactions. Therefore, similar scaling constraints hurt Ethereum demand more than they suppress Bitcoin demand,\u8221\'20\'1D the report read.\par \par \uc2 Other concerns raised about the network included the evolving regulatory status of applications built on Ethereum such as Decentralized Finance (DeFi) and nonfungible tokens (NFTs) which may see strict regulations placed on them in the future, resulting in reduced demand for Ethereum transactions.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/from-morgan-stanley-to-crypto-world-in-a-conversation-with-phemex-founder"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 From Morgan Stanley to crypto world: in a conversation with Phemex founder}}}\par \par \uc2 While the centralization of Ethereum was also highlighted, with the report noting that most of Ether's supply is held by a \u8220\'20\'1Crelatively small number of accounts\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is less decentralized than Bitcoin, with the top 100 addresses holding 39% of Ether, which compares to 14% for Bitcoin.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  side of the equation, the \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  report argued that Ethereum has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-will-replace-bitcoin-as-the-leading-crypto-network-claims-polygon-co-founder"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 greater market potential than Bitcoin}}}\uc2 , it has deflationary traits via its transaction-based burning mechanism, and its performance will significantly improve following the eventual transition to a proof-of-stake consensus mechanism:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEthereum has a much bigger addressable market than Bitcoin and can therefore be worth more than Bitcoin, which is simply the market for store of value products like savings accounts and gold.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDIvNDEwNWQ3ODAtNzQzMC00N2RkLWFmMGUtMTE4MTE2MWZkZmNiLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220218ei2i00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 2/16: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , SOL, AVAX, LUNA, DOGE, DOT\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,819 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 February 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 BTC price is faltering right at the 61.8% Fibonacci Retracement level, triggering a slight pullback in altcoins and sapping the momentum out of this week\u8217\'20\'19s initial breakout to $45,000.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) and the U.S. equity markets are facing selling on Feb. 16 as traders seem to be trimming positions in assets perceived to be risky on the accusation by NATO that Russia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2022/02/16/nato-says-russia-is-increasing-troop-count-at-ukrainian-border.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continues}}}\uc2  to build troops near the Ukrainian border.\par \par \uc2 This is contrary to claims by Moscow that Russian troops are returning to their permanent deployments after completion of the exercise. This geopolitical uncertainty could result in increased \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term.\par \par \uc2 However, the longer-term fundamentals continue to strengthen. PwC Luxembourg, in a recent report, said that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/61-of-luxembourg-financial-players-to-embark-on-crypto-journey-in-2022-pwc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 61% of 123 Luxembourg-based financial players}}}\uc2  have either started or plan to start their \u8220\'20\'1Ccrypto journey\u8221\'20\'1D soon.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/2708bfad-28e2-4c86-9981-54fad541d9f2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/1t-opportunity-jpmorgan-becomes-first-major-bank-in-the-metaverse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JPMorgan has opened a virtual lounge}}}\uc2  in Decentraland\u8217\'20\'19s Metajuku Mall, taking the first step into the metaverse, which the bank believes will present a $1-trillion opportunity.\par \par \uc2 Even Warren Buffet, who has been a vocal critic of Bitcoin until now, seems to be warming up to the fintech sector. \uc2 Berkshire Hathaway\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s security filing shows that the firm has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/warren-buffett-invests-1b-in-bitcoin-friendly-neobank-dumps-visa-and-mastercard-stocks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased its holdings in Nubank}}}\uc2 , the largest fintech bank in Brazil and reduced exposure in Visa and \uc2 Mastercard\uc2  stock.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to determine the near-term price action.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin bounced off the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($41,938) on Feb. 14 but the bulls could not push the price to the overhead resistance at $45,821. This suggests that higher levels continue to attract selling.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/30dd6c8d-7e1f-496e-85af-d54a8234b155.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The moving averages have completed a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the relative strength index (RSI) is in the positive territory, indicating that the sentiment is positive. The bulls are likely to buy the dips to the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns up from the current level or rebounds off the 20-day EMA, the buyers will attempt to drive the price above the neckline of the inverse head and shoulders (H&S) pattern. If they succeed, the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup will complete, signaling a possible reversal.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price breaks below the 20-day EMA, the BTC/USDT pair could drop to $39,600. This is a critical level for the bulls to defend because a break below it could intensify selling.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) broke and closed above the moving averages on Feb. 15, but the bulls are struggling to sustain the price above the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) ($3,068). This indicates that bears continue to sell on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/b1d41e44-ab33-4529-82f3-00ea303ab844.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The sellers will now try to pull the price back below the moving averages. If they succeed, the ETH/USDT pair could drop to the strong support at $2,652.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price rebounds off the moving averages, it will suggest that traders are accumulating on dips. The bulls will then again attempt to drive the price above $3,283.66. A close above this level will complete an inverse H&S pattern, which will indicate the start of a possible up-move. The pair could then rally to $4,000.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) soared above the 20-day EMA ($410) and the downtrend line on Feb. 15 but the bulls could not clear the hurdle at the 50-day SMA ($434).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/3c08ed6d-de4d-438e-82aa-18d0bc31f07c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears are trying to defend the 50-day SMA and pull the price back below the 20-day EMA. If they manage to do that, the aggressive bulls could get trapped and the BNB/USDT pair may drop to $390.60.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the sentiment has turned from sell on rallies to buy on dips. That could increase the possibility of a break above the 50-day SMA. If that happens, the pair may start a rally to the overhead resistance at $500.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) is facing stiff resistance near $0.85 for the past few days. The bears will now try to pull the price to the breakout level at $0.75.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/a4342125-cad6-4173-bea7-41e6d8f32962.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The moving averages have completed a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI is in the positive zone, indicating that bulls have a slight edge. The buyers are likely to defend the 20-day EMA ($0.76) aggressively.\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off this level, the bulls will again attempt to clear the overhead barrier at $0.85. If that happens, the XRP/USDT pair could rise to $0.91 and later to the psychological level at $1. This positive view will invalidate if bears sink and sustain the price below $0.75.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) bounced off the $1 support on Feb. 14 and reached the 20-day EMA ($1.11) on Feb. 15. The bears are unwilling to let go of their advantage and are defending this level aggressively.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/0aac13b0-6fea-4d17-9cff-7777ae631e62.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price remains below the 20-day EMA, the sellers will make one more attempt to sink and sustain the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair below the critical support at $1. Frequent retests of a support level tend to weaken it. If the support cracks, the selling could intensify and the pair could plummet to $0.80.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns up from the current level or $1 and breaks above the moving averages, the pair could reach the resistance line of the channel. The bulls will have to clear this hurdle to signal the start of a new trend.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) bounced on Feb. 14 and reached the 20-day EMA ($105) on Feb. 15 but the bulls are facing stiff resistance from the bears at this level. This indicates that the sentiment remains negative and traders are selling on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/a2c7558c-12d2-4722-a536-b54c00e7b524.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has started to turn down and the RSI is below 43, suggesting that bears have the upper hand. If the selling pressure continues, the SOL/USDT pair could drop to the strong support at $80.83.\par \par \uc2 The bulls are likely to defend this support with vigor. If the price rebounds off this level, the pair could consolidate between $80.83 and $116 for a few days.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns up from the current level and breaks above the 20-day EMA, the pair could rally to the resistance line of the channel. A break and close above the channel will indicate that the downtrend could be over.\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT\par \par \uc2 Avalanche ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ) bounced off the uptrend line on Feb. 14 and surged to the downtrend line on Feb. 15. The bulls pushed the price above the downtrend line on Feb. 16 but the long wick on the candlestick shows that bears are selling at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/b99b1a8d-6401-4b93-af26-b5818c347453.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The moving averages are close to completing a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI is knocking on the overhead resistance near 62. This suggests that bulls have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 If buyers sustain the price above the downtrend line, the AVAX/USDT pair could start a rally to $117.53.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down and breaks below the downtrend line, it will suggest that the current breakout may have been a bear trap. The pair could then again drop to the moving averages. The trend could turn in favor of the bears on a break and close below the uptrend line.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-dips-before-fed-rate-hike-cues-amid-warning-over-9t-balance-sheet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin dips before Fed rate hike cues amid warning over $9T balance sheet}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT\par \par \uc2 Terra\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/terra-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LUNA}}}\uc2  token broke and closed above the 20-day EMA ($56) on Feb. 15, but the bulls are struggling to sustain the higher levels. This suggests that bears continue to sell on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/75fa234d-08b9-4ea4-9201-8e69887ea890.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears have pulled the price back below the 20-day EMA and will now attempt to break the support at $54.20. If that happens, the LUNA/USDT pair could decline to $49.39. If this support also cracks, the next stop could be $43.44.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price rebounds off $54.20, the pair could resume its relief rally to the downtrend line of the descending channel. The bulls will have to push and sustain the price above this resistance to indicate that the downtrend may be over.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) broke and closed above the 20-day EMA ($0.14) on Feb. 15 but the recovery is again facing strong selling at the 50-day SMA ($0.15).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/fc2a6e38-ef60-4986-b1a6-fd3d5ce05787.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the RSI is just below the midpoint, indicating a balance between supply and demand. If bulls push and close the price above the 50-day SMA, the DOGE/USDT pair could challenge the overhead resistance at $0.17. If bulls clear this hurdle, the pair could pick up momentum and rally to $0.22.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price turns down from the current level and plummets below $0.14, the pair could drop to $0.13 and later to the critical support at $0.12.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 The long tail on Polkadot\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) Feb. 14 candlestick shows that bulls are buying on dips near the strong support level at $16.81. The recovery reached the 20-day EMA ($20.16) on Feb. 15 but the bulls could not clear this hurdle.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/f7367f32-3f84-4d16-b543-9ca1f59a9d96.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 This indicates that bears have not yet given up and are mounting a strong defense in the zone between the 20-day EMA and the downtrend line. If the price continues lower, the bears will try to pull the DOT/USDT pair below $16.81 and resume the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price rebounds off $16.81, the pair will again attempt to break above the overhead zone and reach $23.19. A break and close above this resistance will signal a possible change in trend.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDIvMzBhZmQ5ZWEtYjk3Zi00MDc5LTgzNmMtYTk2YTg3MDNjMzNlLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220216ei2g000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 CoinShares\par \b \uc2 Ether investment products register first weekly inflows in 10 weeks\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Sam Bourgi \par \uc2 502 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 February 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Over the past four weeks, inflows into crypto investment products totaled $209 million.\par \par \uc2 Inflows into cryptocurrency investment funds rose sharply last week, with Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) products breaking a nine-week spell of outflows in the latest sign that institutional managers were re-accumulating assets.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  investment products registered $75.3 million worth of cumulative inflows last week, data from \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  revealed Monday. Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) investment products saw $25.1 million worth of inflows, while Ether products attracted $20.9 million worth of capital.\par \par \uc2 Positive inflows were also reported for multi-asset funds with exposure to several cryptocurrencies. Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) and Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) products were also net positive for the week.\par \par \uc2 Crypto asset flows have now risen for four consecutive weeks, offering signs that the massive drawdowns of late 2021 were beginning to reverse course. Over the four-week stretch, crypto funds collected $209 million.\par \par \uc2 Institutional managers reduced their exposure to cryptocurrency products at the end of 2021, possibly to book profits before year\u8217\'20\'19s end and also to ride out {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-kisses-50-day-moving-average-as-trader-predicts-fresh-btc-price-volatility"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extreme market \b  \highlight22volatility\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s Fear & Greed Index, which gauges market sentiment, plunged to \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme fear\u8221\'20\'1D in early January. The Index has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://alternative.me/crypto/fear-and-greed-index/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stabilized}}}\uc2  in recent weeks, with the latest reading showing that the market has exited the extreme fear stage.\par \par \uc2 Are we only in the middle of a large bear cycle?\par \par \uc2 Analyst {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AriRudd?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AriRudd}}}\uc2  notes three indicators that could send Bitcoin to $24K-27K. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AkSAehinSc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/AkSAehinSc}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Cointelegraph (@Cointelegraph) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Cointelegraph/status/1493253902606688262?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 While analysts remain at odds about whether the market has formed a definitive bottom or whether Bitcoin and Ether can expect to re-test their 2022 lows, \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 inflow data provides a good barometer for institutional \b \highlight22\uc2 investor sentiment\b0 \highlight\uc2 . As Cointelegraph has reported, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/the-long-game-institutional-interest-in-crypto-is-just-getting-started"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 institutional demand for crypto assets}}}\uc2  has grown substantially over the past year and is playing a bigger role in influencing market dynamics.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/willy-woo-peak-fear-but-on-chain-metrics-say-it-s-not-a-bear-market"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Willy Woo: \u8216\'20\'18Peak fear,\u8217\'20\'19 but on-chain metrics say it\u8217\'20\'19s not a bear market}}}\par \par \uc2 02/11/22 UPDATE: Net Assets Under Management, Holdings per Share, and Market Price per Share for our Investment Products.\par \par \uc2 Total AUM: $37.6 billion {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BTC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BTC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BAT&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BAT}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BCH&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BCH}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24LINK&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $LINK}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24MANA&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $MANA}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24ETH&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $ETH}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24ETC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $ETC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24FIL&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $FIL}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24ZEN&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $ZEN}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24LTC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $LTC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24LPT&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $LPT}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24XLM&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $XLM}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24ZEC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $ZEC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24UNI&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $UNI}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24AAVE&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $AAVE}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24COMP&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $COMP}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24CRV&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $CRV}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24MKR&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $MKR}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24SUSHI&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $SUSHI}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24SNX&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $SNX}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24YFI&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $YFI}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24ADA&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $\b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24SOL&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $SOL}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24AMP&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $AMP}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/stTPqefvo8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/stTPqefvo8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Grayscale (@Grayscale) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Grayscale/status/1492264248654929923?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Grayscale, which is the largest crypto asset manager, currently has $37.6 billion in assets under management and is looking to convert its flagship GBTC Bitcoin product into an exchange-traded fund (ETF). On Feb. 4, the \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  once again {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-again-delays-decision-on-grayscale-s-bitcoin-etf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-again-delays-decision-on-grayscale-s-bitcoin-etf}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-again-delays-decision-on-grayscale-s-bitcoin-etf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 delayed its decision on Grayscale\u8217\'20\'19s Bitcoin ETF application}}}\uc2 , opening the door to further public comment on the matter.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in Canada, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/canadian-bitcoin-etf-sees-its-third-biggest-daily-inflow-ever"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Purpose Bitcoin ETF}}}\uc2  continues to register large inflows, reflecting strong investor appetite for a spot product.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDIvOTFkNjk3NWEtZDNkNS00MDVmLWI5Y2QtNzE3NTU0ZGU1Y2Y3LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220214ei2e000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 2/14: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , SOL, LUNA, DOGE, AVAX, DOT\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,798 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 February 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 BTC price continues to consolidate, a process which gives altcoin traders the opportunity to range trade and secure short-term gains.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) is attempting to form a higher low as investors take advantage of lower levels to accumulate. \uc2 Twitter\uc2  user PlanC recently highlighted that the balance of addresses having at least two significant incoming transactions but no outgoing transactions has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/up-only-for-btc-fundamentals-5-things-to-watch-in-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 soared to a 57-month high}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, not everyone is \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the future prospects of Bitcoin. Popular analyst Ari Rudd presented {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-bull-trap-3-indicators-that-predict-btc-price-falling-to-24k-27k-this-year"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 three long-term technical setups}}}\uc2 , which point to further downside in Bitcoin. Rudd believes that Bitcoin could offer a buying opportunity in the $24,000 to $27,000 range.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/7839e69f-f4d5-46fd-b17e-1dff49f00600.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Data compiled by Bloomberg {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ca.finance.yahoo.com/news/stocks-swings-exceed-bitcoin-rare-131117301.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shows}}}\uc2  that Bitcoin price has been calmer compared to the Nasdaq 100 Index in 2022. There have been only five occasions this year when Bitcoin has moved more than one standard deviation from its average in either direction, while the Nasdaq 100 has seen 12 such moves.\par \par \uc2 Generally, periods of low \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  are followed by range expansion. Hence, traders may remain cautious because a sharp drop in the Nasdaq 100 could accelerate selling in Bitcoin.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to spot the critical support and resistance levels.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin is attempting to rebound off the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($41,493), indicating that the sentiment has turned positive and traders are buying on dips.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/12f0ec89-a440-4103-9c91-f97f6575bb6c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls will attempt to push and sustain the price above the overhead resistance at $45,821. If they manage to do that, the BTC/USDT pair will complete a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  inverse head and shoulders pattern.\par \par \uc2 The pair could first rally to the psychological level at $50,000 and if this level is crossed, the rally may reach the stiff overhead resistance at $52,088.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the current level or the overhead resistance, it will suggest that bears continue to sell on rallies. The pair could then drop to $39,600. The bears will have to pull the price below this support to gain the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) plunged below the 20-day EMA ($2,934) and re-entered the descending channel on Feb. 11, indicating selling at higher levels. A minor positive is that the price has been clinging to the 20-day EMA in the past two days.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/ba3965da-6ae9-4745-bde4-211a584fabe4.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The flattish 20-day EMA and the relative strength index (RSI) just below the midpoint suggest a balance between supply and demand. If the price breaks and sustains above the 20-day EMA, the buyers will make one more attempt to push the ETH/USDT pair above the overhead resistance zone at $3,283.66 to $3,411.43.\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the pair will complete an inverted H&S pattern. This reversal setup has a target objective at $4,408.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price once again turns down from the overhead resistance, it will suggest that bears continue to sell on rallies. That will increase the prospects of a drop to the strong support at $2,652.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) broke and closed below the 20-day EMA ($407) on Feb. 11, indicating that traders who bought at lower levels may be booking profits.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/c07ecd5f-d90d-47a3-a031-cb8d2383fa44.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 However, a minor positive is that the bulls have not allowed the bears to have their way and are buying the dips below $400. The 20-day EMA is flat but the RSI has dropped near 47, suggesting a minor edge to the bears.\par \par \uc2 If the price sustains below $400, the possibility of a drop to $347.40 increases. This negative view will invalidate if the BNB/USDT pair turns up from the current level and breaks above the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) ($439). The pair could then start its journey toward the psychological level at $500.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ripple\u8217\'20\'19s (XRP) sharp rebound off the breakout level at $0.75 turned down from $0.85, indicating that bears are selling on rallies. The bears will now attempt to pull the price below $0.75.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/00b4f189-6e08-4e0a-a44d-8072c1c01d5e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they manage to do that, the selling could intensify as traders who bought at lower levels or on a break above $0.75 may rush to the exit. That could pull the XRP/USDT pair to $0.65 and then to $0.60.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price rises from the current level or rebounds off $0.75, it will suggest that bulls are accumulating near the breakout level. The buyers will then make one more attempt to resume the up-move by pushing the price above the $0.85 to $0.91 resistance zone.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) broke below the 20-day EMA ($1.11) on Feb. 11 and has reached strong support at $1. The repeated retest of a support level tends to weaken it.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/e0578a2a-1245-48ca-9496-85fe9662bf79.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The downsloping moving averages and the RSI in the negative territory indicate that bears are in control. A break and close below $1 could signal the resumption of the downtrend. The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could then drop to $0.80.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if bulls once again manage to defend the $1 support, the pair will attempt to rally above the moving averages. The buyers will have to push and sustain the price above the channel to indicate a possible change in trend.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) continues to trade inside the descending channel pattern and is gradually correcting toward the strong support at $80.83. The 20-day EMA ($106) has started to turn down once again and the RSI is in the negative territory, indicating that bears have the upper hand.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/b7fd6ed3-348c-47ec-8824-732acc4ad29c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The SOL/USDT pair could now slide to the strong support at $80.83. This is an important level to watch out for because if it cracks, the selling could intensify and the pair could drop to the support line of the channel.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price turns up from the current level or rebounds off $80.83, the bulls will try to push the pair to the resistance line of the channel. A break and close above this level will be the first sign that the downtrend could be over.\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT\par \par \uc2 Terra\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/terra-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LUNA}}}\uc2  token has been trading below $54.20 for the past three days but a minor positive is that the bulls have not allowed the price to break and sustain below the psychological level at $50.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/1f7c239a-8af0-4c97-aa94-d60c7e82967f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The first sign of strength will be a break and close above the 20-day EMA ($56), which will indicate that the bears may be losing their grip. The bulls will then attempt to push the price to the downtrend line of the descending channel where the bears may again pose a stiff challenge.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if bulls fail to push the price above the 20-day EMA within the next few days, the selling could intensify and the LUNA/USDT pair could slide toward the strong support at $43.44. The downsloping moving averages and the RSI in the negative territory indicate that bears have a slight advantage.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-kisses-50-day-moving-average-as-trader-predicts-fresh-btc-price-volatility"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin kisses 50-day moving average as trader predicts fresh BTC price \b  \highlight22volatility\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin (DOGE) broke and closed below the 20-day EMA ($0.14) on Feb. 11. Attempts by the bulls to reclaim the level failed on Feb. 12 as the price turned down from the 50-day SMA ($0.15).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/17927c7e-5a60-4331-b36a-fde999e000bb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA is flattish but the RSI has dipped below 47, indicating that bears are attempting to gain the upper hand. If sellers sink the price below $0.14, the DOGE/USDT pair may decline to the critical support at $0.12.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns up from the current level and breaks above the moving averages, it will suggest that bulls are accumulating on dips. The buyers will then try to push the pair above $0.17 and extend the up-move to $0.22.\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT\par \par \uc2 Avalanche ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the downtrend line on Feb. 10 and has dipped to the uptrend line, indicating that the traders who bought at lower levels may be exiting their positions.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/63026227-afb4-46ab-b333-4eb46b6bc871.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($79) is flat and the RSI is just above the midpoint, indicating a balance between supply and demand. If the price breaks and sustains below $75.50, the possibility of a drop to $64.85 and then to $61 increases.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price rebounds off the current level, the bulls will again try to drive the price above the downtrend line. If they succeed, it will signal that the downtrend could be over. The pair could then rise to $100 and later to $117.53.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the downtrend line on Feb. 8 and could now drop to the strong support at $16.81. Both moving averages have started to turn down and the RSI is in the negative territory, indicating that bears are in command.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/6b646160-0a68-440e-948b-693b4e6c42b1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If bears pull the price below $16.81, the selling could pick up further and the DOT/USDT pair could drop to the next major support at $10.37. Contrary to this assumption, if the price rebounds off the current level or $16.81, the bulls will attempt to push the pair above the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 If they manage to do that, the pair could rise to the overhead resistance at $23.19. If the price turns down from this level, the pair could remain range-bound for a few more days. The bulls are likely to gain the upper hand on a break and close above $23.19.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDIvYmE5ZDNhZDYtODViMi00MTcyLTlhYTctNmZkMmJlMGJhZDA2LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220214ei2e000b7\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s shaping the future of the institutional crypto market?\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Christophe Michot \par \uc2 1,390 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 February 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Infrastructure improvements, trading volume growth and new tools and services reflect the ongoing maturation of the institutional crypto market.\par \par \uc2 2021 was a big year for cryptocurrency. El Salvador {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/inside-el-salvador-s-bitcoin-experiment-cointelegraph-video-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 became the first country to adopt}}}\uc2  Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) as legal tender. In November 2021, the price of Bitcoin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/suddenly-bitcoin-hits-new-all-time-high-after-2k-gains-in-minutes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hit an all-time high}}}\uc2  approaching the psychologically significant mark of $70,000. And, all along the way, industry influencers like Elon Musk have been tweeting their enthusiasm about cryptocurrency more broadly.\par \par \uc2 I anticipate 2022 will continue to be an even bigger year for digital currencies as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/staying-cool-is-crypto-snowballing-to-1-billion-users-this-year"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 market grows to reach}}}\uc2  1 billion people. Here are the five most prominent trends that I see on the horizon for the year to come.\par \par \uc2 Institutional trading volume will grow\par \par \uc2 2022 will be a year in which institutional and retail cryptocurrency adoption, and trading in particular, will continue to grow. Fintech stalwarts \uc2 PayPal\uc2  and Square \u8212\'20\'14 along with mobile stock-trading platform Robinhood \u8212\'20\'14 have all made it easier to buy, sell and trade crypto. And public companies like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/microstrategy-buys-the-dip-by-purchasing-660-bitcoin-for-25m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MicroStrategy}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/tesla-held-2b-of-bitcoin-as-of-late-2021-sec-filing-reveals"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tesla}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/invest-in-bitcoin-galaxy-digital-ad-tells-financial-times-readers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Galaxy}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/jack-dorsey-s-square-adds-4-709-bitcoin-to-its-balance-sheet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Square}}}\uc2  all added significant amounts of Bitcoin to their balance sheets in 2021.\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s driving this growth? Aside from upward general momentum, two pieces of evidence reflect the ongoing maturity of the institutional crypto market: market cap and infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 In 2015, the total crypto market cap was around $5 billion. As of December 2021, it\u8217\'20\'19s grown enormously to above $2 trillion. Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s market cap alone {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/historical/20150104/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was}}}\uc2  $3.6 billion on Jan. 4, 2015, and its current market cap {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/bitcoin/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is}}}\uc2  around $900 billion. Even the market cap of number two crypto, Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ), which has a bigger ecosystem of enterprise applications, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/ethereum/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 around}}}\uc2  $400 billion, which is close to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/V?p=V&.tsrc=fin-srch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Visa}}}\uc2  or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/JPM/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JP Morgan Chase}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/306db99b-d438-46c4-b2b3-912d410a1dec.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Even five years ago, core infrastructure was much less developed in crypto. Institutions were struggling to understand how to custody, trade and clear and settle crypto transactions in a reliable, compliant way. There weren\u8217\'20\'19t any true prime brokers in crypto. Now the infrastructure is much more developed and institutions have a better understanding and comfort level with the crypto landscape. As such, I anticipate institutional trading will continue to grow.\par \par \uc2 Even so, spot crypto trading volume, especially Bitcoin, is still highly fragmented.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/95f2a04a-3d4c-445f-ac08-b8f6eed06034.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Institutional adoption will also accelerate the growth of the crypto derivatives market. More \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2  will come too, which will be a very positive development as long as it involves public discourse and is tailored for industry products to allow for adoption and innovation while also meeting regulators\u8217\'20\'19 needs.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/explained/what-should-the-crypto-industry-expect-from-regulators-in-2022-experts-answer-part-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What should the crypto industry expect from regulators in 2022? Experts answer, Part 1}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/explained/what-should-the-crypto-industry-expect-from-regulators-in-2022-experts-answer-part-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Part 2}}}\par \par \uc2 In July 2021, Treasury Secretary Janet Yellen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/treasury-secretary-yellen-urges-lawmakers-to-quickly-introduce-stablecoin-guidelines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged regulators to act quickly}}}\uc2  to create a regulatory framework for stablecoins. Since then, U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) Chairman Gary Gensler {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-chair-wants-robust-crypto-regulatory-regime-for-the-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has also called for \b  \highlight22regulation\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in this space and indicated this is on the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s agenda.\par \par \uc2 More institutional service providers and tools will come to market\par \par \uc2 Still, institutions have a critical need for the right services and tools. There\u8217\'20\'19s been a flurry of activity among startups looking to provide support services, such as crypto asset storage, security and management and investment products, as well as mining hardware and software and payment infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 Multiple companies had raised funding rounds of at least $300 million by August 2021, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/blockchain-com-raises-300m-in-crypto-industry-s-third-largest-capital-raise"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Blockchain.com}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-lending-firm-blockfi-raises-350m-in-new-funding-round"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BlockFi}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/blockchain-unicorn-fireblocks-raises-310m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fireblocks}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/wallet-provider-ledger-raises-380m-to-welcome-defi-ecosystem"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ledger}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/paypal-crypto-partner-paxos-raises-300m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Paxos}}}\uc2 . I expect this to continue as new companies emerge to provide more accessibility into the crypto market than ever before. This, in turn, will open new doors for small and medium-sized funds.\par \par \uc2 Altcoins will become more popular\par \par \uc2 Next year I also expect to see altcoins grow in popularity as enthusiasts learn even more about their various use cases. Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ), for example, is driven by DApp development with a robust ecosystem. However, due to Ethereum\u8217\'20\'19s scalability issues and high gas fees, it has also become challenged by blockchain upstarts like Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) and Avalanche ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ). Investors see huge growth opportunities, while traders see \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  and cross-pair arbitrage opportunities.\par \par \uc2 More broadly, I anticipate altcoins will become more popular as investors seek ways to diversify their crypto portfolios. A report from Nasdaq {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nasdaq.com/articles/8-potential-contenders-to-become-the-next-big-crypto-king-2021-10-22"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2  that as of October 2021, there were more than 100 altcoins valued at more than $1 billion, which \u8220\'20\'1C[implies] a flourishing digital ecosystem.\u8221\'20\'1D While altcoin prices can be similarly volatile \u8212\'20\'14 and investors should do their research first \u8212\'20\'14 many altcoins, including Solana and Polkadot, continue to top lists of cryptocurrencies with the most potential to become the next big thing.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/when-and-why-did-the-word-altcoin-lose-its-relevance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 When and why did the word 'altcoin' lose its relevance?}}}\par \par \uc2 Volume will shift away from Bitcoin into the altcoin Ether and is even now starting to shift. For further proof, look to digital currency asset manager Grayscale Investments, which recently expanded its portfolio of investment products to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/solana-price-eyes-300-as-grayscale-launches-sol-backed-trust"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 include a trust focused}}}\uc2  on Solana.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have had a front row seat to the mainstream acceptance and adoption of crypto and increasingly find that investors are diversifying their exposure beyond digital assets like Bitcoin and Ethereum,\u8221\'20\'1D Grayscale CEO \uc2 Michael Sonnenshein{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.globenewswire.com/fr/news-release/2021/11/30/2343063/0/en/Grayscale-Investments-Launches-Grayscale-Solana-Trust.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in a recent statement, adding:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur family of Grayscale products will continue to expand alongside this exciting asset class, as we remain committed to offering investors opportunities to access the digital economy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Regulated DeFi for institutions is coming\par \par \uc2 Decentralized finance, or the emerging ecosystem of financial applications that use blockchain technology, will have a big year in 2022. The total value locked (TVL) in DeFi grew significantly in 2021.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/4f6b74dc-3e96-4224-b420-930b8a97d7bb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 To date, institutions have remained on the DeFi sidelines because counterparties in DeFi transactions are largely unknown. Whether an institution wants to be a liquidity provider (LP) or trade on a decentralized exchange (DEX), regulatory clarity and compliance are paramount. This is why Aave {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/aave-launches-its-permissioned-pool-aave-arc-with-30-institutions-set-to-join"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launched a permissioned DeFi platform}}}\uc2 , Aave Arc.\par \par \uc2 In most DEXs, LPs do not have to pass compliance checks such as Know Your Customer and Anti-Money Laundering requirements. Looking forward to 2022, I expect DeFi growth to accelerate. Two challenges will likely be addressed: lack of regulatory clarity and lack of counterparty compliance checks.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/explained/from-defi-year-to-decade-is-mass-adoption-here-experts-answer-part-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 From DeFi year to decade: Is mass adoption here? Experts answer, Part 1}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/explained/from-defi-year-to-decade-is-mass-adoption-here-experts-answer-part-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Part 2}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/explained/from-defi-year-to-decade-is-mass-adoption-here-experts-answer-part-3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Part 3}}}\par \par \uc2 More regulatory clarity is likely to emerge as the SEC and other regulatory bodies provide new guidance. And new DeFi platforms for institutions will gain traction. These platforms will require LPs and traders to pass compliance checks and will provide sufficient liquidity for institutions.\par \par \uc2 With more clarity and the right platforms in place, more institutions will enter the DeFi space.\par \par \uc2 Security solutions will become more prevalent\par \par \uc2 Hacks have long been a part of crypto\u8217\'20\'19s history. In 2014, for example, Bitcoin exchange \uc2 Mt. Gox\uc2  filed for bankruptcy after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/crypto-exchange-hacks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hackers reportedly stole}}}\uc2  millions of U.S. dollars. Four years later, hackers stole from another cryptocurrency exchange, Coincheck. And in August 2021, DeFi platform {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/hackers-stole-at-least-600m-in-poly-exploit-across-three-chains"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Poly Network lost $600 million}}}\uc2  to hackers. MonoX Finance, another DeFi platform, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/defi-disasters-31m-drained-from-monox-and-badgerdao-losses-top-120m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost $31 million}}}\uc2  even more recently.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/crypto-exchange-hacks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Report on crypto exchange hacks: 2011\u8211\'20\'132020}}}\par \par \uc2 Now, crypto exchanges are starting to make moves to protect themselves and tend to partner with qualified custodians to manage custody risks. For example, \uc2 Coinbase{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/coinbase-will-establish-presence-in-israel-through-purchase-of-unbound-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 acquired cryptographic security company}}}\uc2  Unbound Security in November 2021 to enhance its multi-party computational capabilities. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/paypal-purchases-crypto-custody-firm-curv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 PayPal also acquired}}}\uc2  another \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  security provider, Curv. I expect to see similar deals throughout 2022.\par \par \uc2 The crypto industry moves fast with many twists and turns. But one thing is sure: The signposts for 2022 point to continued growth.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 The views, thoughts and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par \uc2 Christophe Michot is the director of business development at Apifiny, a global \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading network for institutions. Before Apifiny, Michot was a senior manager at Kraken and Apple, and a \uc2 Google\uc2  alumnus. Michot brings over 20 years of experience in the tech industry, including 10 years dedicated to Bitcoin and crypto.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjItMDIvMDIxNDg2MDctMTE3ZS00ZDY5LThkZDMtMmRjMmJhMGQxMmMxLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020220213ei2d00003\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 2/11: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , SOL, LUNA, AVAX, DOT, DOGE\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,826 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 February 2022\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2022. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The tight range trading in Bitcoin and select altcoins suggests that bulls and bears are battling it out to gain the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) is attempting to bottom out and whales seem to be helping it do that. Coin Metrics data shows that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-s-30-recovery-in-two-weeks-has-btc-whales-back-in-accumulation-mode"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 whale addresses holding at least 1,000 Bitcoin}}}\uc2  have been accumulating in the past few days. The total supply of these addresses rose from 7.95 million Bitcoin on Jan. 24 to 8.096 million on Feb. 10.\par \par \uc2 Another sign that \b \highlight22\uc2 investor sentiment\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be turning positive is that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/exchange-stablecoin-reserve-hits-27b-as-bitcoin-rises-toward-50k-fair-value"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crypto exchange balances of stablecoins have soared}}}\uc2  above $27 billion for the first time, according to on-chain analytics platform CryptoQuant. In comparison, Bitcoin reserves on the exchanges have continued to slide, indicating that investors are stashing their holdings.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/5db69acd-3070-4c5c-b714-d1e0e6f99e0a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Although Bitcoin has been closely correlated with the U.S. equity markets in the short term, Zhu Su, co-founder of hedge fund Three Arrows Capital (3AC), believes their performance will diverge in 2022. Zhu suggested that Bitcoin and Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/blackrock-expected-to-offer-crypto-trading-as-three-arrows-exec-says-long-bitcoin-eth-in-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 candidates for going long}}}\uc2  while the S&P 500 is a short candidate.\par \par \uc2 After the recent recovery in Bitcoin and altcoins, is it time for a minor correction or consolidation? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin turned down from the overhead resistance at $45,456 on Feb. 10, indicating that bulls continue to defend the level aggressively. A minor positive is that bulls have not allowed the price to break below the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) ($42,427).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/8f03b62a-2521-4657-bccc-ae14bb21f8a4.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 This indicates that bulls are attempting to flip the 50-day SMA into support. The rising 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($41,317) and the relative strength index (RSI) in positive territory indicate a slight advantage to buyers.\par \par \uc2 If the price bounces off the current level, the bulls will make one more attempt to push the BTC/USDT pair above $45,456. If they succeed, the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum could pick up and the pair may rise to $48,000 and later to $52,088.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the current level or from $45,456, the bears will fancy their chances and attempt to pull the pair below the 20-day EMA. If that happens, the pair could drop to $39,600.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether broke and closed above the 50-day SMA ($3,171) on Feb. 9, but the bulls could not build upon this strength. The price turned back below the 50-day SMA on Feb. 10, which suggests that bears are attempting to trap the aggressive bulls.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/c14d49d9-e4ee-4d0d-b6ed-05ad6a79b8ca.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 However, a positive sign is that the bulls have not allowed the price to break back into the channel. If the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA ($2,959), the buyers will again attempt to push the ETH/USDT pair above the overhead hurdle.\par \par \uc2 The zone between the 50-day SMA and $3,400 could act as a major roadblock. If buyers clear this hurdle, the pair could start a new up-move\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price re-enters the channel, it will suggest that sentiment remains negative and traders are selling on rallies. The pair could then drop to the critical support at $2,652.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) is struggling to break above the downtrend line of the descending channel. This suggests that bears are defending the resistance with all their might.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/3e691501-4484-4696-ac8d-1cd485f4e9a5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The flattish 20-day EMA ($410) and the RSI near the midpoint suggest a balance between supply and demand. If the price breaks below the 20-day EMA, it will increase the prospects of the BNB/USDT pair staying inside the channel for a few more days. The pair could first slip to $390 and then continue its downward move to $357.40.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price rebounds off the current level, the bulls will make one more attempt to propel the pair above the channel and the 50-day SMA ($448). If they succeed, the pair could gradually rise to $500.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) is witnessing profit-booking after the recent rally. The price could drop to the breakout level at $0.75 where the buyers may step in to arrest the decline.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/65576840-fd60-49b4-89c7-0c3f6915acb9.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The rising 20-day EMA ($0.73) and the RSI in the positive territory indicate that bulls have the upper hand. The buyers will now attempt to defend the support at $0.75.\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off this level, the buyers will again attempt to drive the XRP/USDT pair above $0.92 and challenge the psychological resistance at $1.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will invalidate in the short term if the price breaks below the 20-day EMA. Such a move could open the doors for a decline to $0.65.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) has repeatedly failed to break above the 50-day SMA ($1.22) in the past few days, indicating that bears are defending this level with vigor. The sellers will now attempt to sink and sustain the price below the 20-day EMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/c720d12b-1b60-4658-b450-cb1605de95c9.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they manage to do that, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could drop to the critical support at $1. This is an important level for the bulls to defend because a break and close below it could intensify selling. The pair could then slide to $0.80.\par \par \uc2 The moving averages have flattened out and the RSI is near the midpoint, indicating a balance between supply and demand. If the price bounces off the current level and breaks above the 50-day SMA, the pair could rise to the resistance line of the descending channel. A break and close above this level will signal a positive change in trend.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the overhead resistance at $116 and broke back below the 20-day EMA ($111) on Feb. 10. This suggests that the sentiment remains negative and bears are selling on rallies to resistance levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/64a8cd30-ec05-419e-9b00-251df7a8a312.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The SOL/USDT pair could now slide to $94 and then to the strong support at $80.83. This is an important level for the bulls to defend because a break and close below it could signal the resumption of the downtrend. The pair could then drop to the support line of the channel.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of a trend change will happen on a break and close above the resistance line of the channel. Such a move could signal the start of a possible new uptrend. The pair could then rally to $157.80.\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls have repeatedly failed to push Terra\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/terra-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LUNA}}}\uc2  token above the 20-day EMA ($57.80) in the past few days, which suggests that bears are defending the level aggressively. Hence, this becomes a key resistance to watch on the upside.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/8eaae08e-ab6a-4aa4-9b9a-a200c65c1f1c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI in the negative territory indicate that bears have the upper hand. If the price sustains below $54.20, the LUNA/USDT pair could slip down to the strong support at $43.44.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will invalidate if the price turns up from the current level and breaks above $60.64. The pair could then rally to the downtrend line of the descending channel where the bears may again pose a strong challenge to buyers.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-stuck-in-a-tight-range-as-btc-price-moving-averages-prepare-key-bullish-cross"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin stuck in a tight range as BTC price moving averages prepare key \b  \highlight22bullish\b0 \highlight22  cross}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT\par \par \uc2 The downtrend line is proving to be a tough barrier for the bulls to cross. This indicates that higher levels continue to attract selling by the bears. If Avalanche ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ) breaks below the 50-day SMA ($87), a drop to the 20-day EMA ($80) is possible.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/e92c57af-8ce9-4ab0-bb04-0ecb70467e1c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that traders are buying on dips. The bulls will then again try to thrust the price above the downtrend line and start a new up-move. If they manage to do that, the AVAX/USDT pair could rally to $117.53.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price breaks below the support zone between the 20-day EMA and $75.50, it will suggest that the sentiment remains negative and traders are selling on rallies. The pair could then drop to $64.85.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) slipped and closed below the 20-day EMA ($20.96) on Feb. 10, indicating that bears are aggressively defending the overhead resistance zone between $22.66 and the 50-day SMA ($23.75).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-02/ab4ef3a1-b5fa-4c59-89d5-d82447f49ac6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The flattish moving averages and the RSI below 46 suggest that bears have a slight edge in the short term. If the price sustains below the 20-day EMA, the DOT/USDT pair could slide to the strong support at $16.81. If the price rebounds off this support, the pair could remain range-bound for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns up from 